port you and your loved ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career growth</strong> 📈 – We hire rising stars who grow with us! You’ll get €1K (or equivalent) per year to spend on courses, books, events, or coaching to level up your skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A passionate team</strong> 🤩 – We love our product, and we prove it with regular hackathons where we see who can build the coolest thing with it!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first</strong> 🌏 – Our team works remotely across Europe, with regular off-sites for team bonding. Some roles, like sales in the US, are hybrid—please check the job description.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Giving back</strong> 🤝 – We're big fans of open source, and you'll get $100 per month to support projects you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency</strong> 🙏 – We all know what everyone’s working on, how the company is doing—the whole shebang.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Country and/or State specific details provided in your employment agreement.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/n8n/internal-context-engineer-berlin-422357","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin Office","created_at":1792021227},{"slug":"internal-ai-enablement-lead-berlin-118279","company_name":"N8N","title":"Internal AI Enablement Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. We give technical teams the freedom of code with the speed of no-code, so they can automate faster, smarter, and without limits. Backed by a fiercely inventive community and 500+ builder-approved integrations, we’re changing the way people bring systems together and scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><h3>🎯 Your main goal will be to turn n8n’s internal AI and automation capabilities into something every function can confidently use, build with, and learn from.</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">To make that happen, you’ll create the programs, experiences, and foundations that help teams across n8n build their AI and automation fluency:</p><h3>DRIVE HANDS-ON ENABLEMENT</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run weekly, role-specific workshops, prioritizing less-technical functions such as Legal and Customer Support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead hands-on sessions where you build live alongside teams, helping them turn real workflows and challenges into working automations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run Build Along Office Hours and Bounty Hunts that give teams regular opportunities to learn, experiment, and solve problems together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help teams identify useful automation opportunities, understand the process they are changing, and decide when to reuse an existing solution, build themselves, or involve the Automation team.</p></li></ul><h3>OWN DOGFOODING &amp; EXPERIMENTATION</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our monthly Dogfooding Day end-to-end, from planning and coordination through execution and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and run hackathons and other experimentation initiatives that encourage teams to explore new ways of working with AI and automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn learnings and outputs from these initiatives into reusable assets that help other teams move faster.</p></li></ul><h3>SCALE AI FLUENCY &amp; COMMUNITY</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own periodic AI fluency survey cycles alongside the People team and help calibrate what fluency means across different functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build visibility around internal wins and reusable solutions so teams can learn from what others have already created.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and support champions across functions, informally leading the emerging Guild and helping automation knowledge spread across the company.</p></li></ul><h3>ENABLE SAFE, REUSABLE AUTOMATION</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as product owner for our internal “safe playground,” partnering with IT, Security, Data, and Solutions Engineering on access, credentials, environments, and requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn outputs from workshops and office hours into reusable templates and resources that teams can easily discover and adopt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively help teams reuse existing solutions rather than reinventing them, making automation more accessible and scalable across n8n.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check whether the things built are still in use four weeks later; provide evidence that teams reuse existing assets and can make routine changes without handing everything back to the Automation team.</p></li></ul><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ Practitioner-level n8n fluency:</strong> You’ve built real, meaningful automations in n8n and are comfortable building live alongside others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎓 Technical enablement experience:</strong> You’ve run structured, recurring enablement programs such as workshops, office hours, or build-alongs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Non-technical audience expertise:</strong> You have a strong track record of helping non-technical teams understand, adopt, and confidently use technical tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏗️ Cross-functional ownership:</strong> You’re comfortable partnering with IT, Security, and Data teams to define and own requirements around access, credentials, and environments without needing to implement the infrastructure yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌍 CET overlap:</strong> You’re based in a time zone that gives you strong overlap with Central European working hours, within a couple of hours of Berlin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💬 English fluency:</strong> You have fluent or near-native English and can communicate clearly and confidently with audiences ranging from individual contributors to senior stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em">