scale ideas for impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our founding in 2019, we’ve grown into a diverse team of over 260 - working across Europe and the US, connected by a shared builder spirit and with our centre of gravity in Berlin. Along the way, we’ve:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivated a community of more than 650,000 active developers and builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earned 190K+ GitHub stars, making us one of the world’s Top 40 most popular projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top investors, from Sequoia’s first German seed to our SAP's recent strategic investment - bringing us to a $5.2bn valuation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />That’s the company we’ve built. Now we’d love to see what <em>you </em>can build. If you’re applying, try n8n out - whether you’re technical or not - and share a screenshot of your first workflow with us. The easiest place to start is here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://app.n8n.cloud/register"><u>app.n8n.cloud/register</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in a defining moment of an incredible journey. Come and build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎯 Your main goal will be to <strong>identify and reduce security risks across n8n's product and internal systems</strong>, using threat modelling, hands-on security expertise, and cross-functional collaboration to help teams design, build, and operate more secure systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join our growing security team at a pivotal stage, acting as a trusted security partner to teams across the business. You'll help us build a move from reactive security management to a proactive, scalable security practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here's what you'll be driving:</p><h3>Threat Modelling, Risk Assessment &amp; Security Design</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct threat modelling and risk assessments across product features, AI agents, cloud infrastructure, corporate IT, internal applications, and data systems, identifying vulnerabilities and recommending practical mitigations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Engineering, Cloud, IT, and Data teams to review security designs, define actionable security requirements, and influence the implementation of appropriate controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help teams embed security into their development processes through secure coding guidance, design reviews, documentation, and security tooling that enables them to identify and address risks independently.</p></li></ul><h3>Vulnerability Management &amp; Coordinated Disclosure</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in the security triage rotation, assessing incoming vulnerability reports, validating findings, and prioritising remediation based on severity and business impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with engineering teams to coordinate vulnerability remediation, verify fixes, and support secure patch and release processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help manage our vulnerability disclosure and bug bounty programmes, including engagement with security researchers, coordinated disclosures, and GitHub Security Advisories.</p></li></ul><h3>Security Operations &amp; Incident Readiness</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help establish and improve logging, detection, and protective monitoring capabilities across our infrastructure, corporate systems, and internal applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and improve incident response processes, runbooks, and exercises to strengthen our ability to detect, investigate, and respond to security incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with system owners to identify security gaps, prioritise remediation, and verify that implemented controls effectively reduce risk.</p></li></ul><h3>Customer Trust &amp; Compliance Engineering</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support SOC 2 compliance by helping establish continuous control monitoring, automated evidence collection, and processes that make security assurance part of everyday operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Sales, Solutions Engineering, and Customer Success to respond to customer security assessments and build reusable resources that streamline future requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Legal, Finance, IT, and other stakeholders to assess security risks, improve security policies and controls, and strengthen trust with enterprise customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We're hiring two Security Engineers with complementary strengths, so you don't need to be an expert in every security domain. </strong></p><h2>REQUIREMENTS</h2><h3><strong>Must-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔍 Threat Modelling &amp; Risk Assessment:</strong> You have hands-on experience assessing real-world systems, identifying security risks, determining defensible severity levels, and recommending practical controls that teams can implement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ Technical Security Expertise:</strong> You can validate security findings, reproduce vulnerabilities, develop proof-of-concepts, and write code or automation when needed to demonstrate risks or improve security processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔐 Security Engineering Experience:</strong> You've worked hands-on in infrastructure, product, or application security within a product-focused organisation, with a strong understanding of how modern systems are designed and secured.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Cross-functional Influence:</strong> You're comfortable acting as an internal security consultant, advising teams, challenging technical decisions constructively, and influencing stakeholders without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎯 Risk Remediation &amp; Ownership:</strong> You've helped secure systems you don't directly own, translating security findings into actionable requirements and working with responsible teams to ensure effective remediation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤖 AI &amp; LLM Fluency:</strong> You're comfortable using LLM-assisted tooling and understand its limitations, security implications, and potential failure modes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✍️ Clear Communication:</strong> You can explain complex security risks, document technical findings, and provide practical guidance that engineers and non-technical stakeholders can confidently act on.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You also bring deep expertise in at least two of the following areas:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💻 Application Security:</strong> You've developed security checks, engineering guardrails, tooling, or guidance that helps product teams build and ship secure software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>☁️ Platform Security:</strong> You have experience securing a major cloud provider and Kubernetes environments, including areas such as sandboxing, multi-tenancy, or identity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔑 Corporate Security:</strong> You've worked on identity and access management, endpoint security, employee access lifecycles, or data access controls across corporate environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚨 Security Monitoring:</strong> You've implemented logging, protective monitoring, or security detection capabilities that support effective investigation and incident response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📋 Security Assurance &amp; Compliance:</strong> You've supported SOC 2 or ISO 27001 from an engineering perspective, including implementing technical controls or automating compliance evidence collection.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🐛 Vulnerability Disclosure:</strong> You've helped operate bug bounty or coordinated vulnerability disclosure programmes, including publishing security advisories such as GHSAs or CVEs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 AI &amp; Agent Security:</strong> You have experience assessing or securing LLM-powered applications and AI agents, including risks related to permissions, tool access, prompt injection, or sensitive data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏢 Corporate IT Tooling:</strong> You're familiar with platforms such as Okta, Azure, or Drata and their role in securing corporate systems and supporting compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌍 Open-source Ecosystems:</strong> You've worked with open-source or source-available products, contributed to security communities, or are already familiar with n8n.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎯 Penetration Testing:</strong> You have practical penetration testing experience and can independently identify, demonstrate, and help remediate security vulnerabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌱 Early-stage Security Experience:</strong> You've been an early security hire or helped establish security practices in a startup or rapidly scaling organisation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At n8n, you'll help shape security at a defining stage of our growth. We're building a security practice that goes beyond reacting to vulnerabilities, and you'll play a key role in how we i