nd market access to become even more successful: <strong>adjoe</strong> is developing a breakthrough mobile advertising solution that enables app publishers around the world to grow their advertising revenues. <strong>justDice</strong> is the market leader in Mobile Gaming Loyalty Programs. <strong>Sunday</strong> is a next-generation hybrid casual mobile game publisher. And <strong>justtrack</strong> offers unique software to automate the entire mobile user acquisition process. Yet more to come.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Under the umbrella of the media company <strong>Bertelsmann</strong>, we have access to a global network of experts and strong financial support. By developing a state-of-the-art tech stack and highly skilled workforce, we aim to reach more mobile users than any other company in the world. If you want to grow your career in tech, challenge yourself in a high-performance environment, while having fun with great colleagues from all over the world, you've come to the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find the whole world in one office. Boost your career with awesome people!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will do:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR Partnership:</strong> Serve as the dedicated HR Partner and trusted advisor for assigned subsidiaries, departments, and Leads equally across all of our employees’ locations - striving for high level of engagement among employees and managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Managerial Consultation:</strong> Consult managers on the full employee lifecycle, proactive performance management and labor law matters, ensuring the right balance HR excellence and using a pragmatic approach in every step.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance Enablement: </strong>Upskill managers on early-stage performance management, considering legal compliance but also high-speed, pragmatic, tactical support to minimize business disruption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conflict Resolution &amp; Compliance:</strong> Independently manage and resolve standard employee relations issues, performance exits, and disciplinary actions, coordinating between HR and Business Leads, as well as consulting with external legal support on sensitive or unprecedented cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual HR Cycles:</strong> Co-steer, execute, and continuously improve key recurring HR processes within your scope, such as performance review and compensation cycles, as well as engagement surveys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Liaison:</strong> Act as the central driver for collaboration with Talent Acquisition, Payroll, IT, Office, Finance, Legal, and external authorities to guarantee slick, frictionless end-to-end HR service delivery and employee engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR Innovation &amp; Projects:</strong> Initiate and steer cross-company HR projects focused on improving collaboration and elevating our global employer value proposition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 3–5 years of experience in a generalistic, consultative HR role, ideally within a fast-paced, dynamic, or growth tech environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> University degree in Business Administration, HR Management, Psychology, Law, or a completed relevant apprenticeship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Labor Law Expertise:</strong> Strong, tested knowledge of German/International labor law, and modern employee management practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder Management:</strong> Proven track record of successfully advising, challenging, and building trust with) business leads across various hierarchical levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifecycle &amp; Global Mobility:</strong> Profound experience in full HR lifecycle management, including dealing with international relocation and immigration cases, as well as EOR services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tech &amp; Tool Savviness:</strong> High proficiency in modern HRIS platforms (e.g., Personio, Workday) and digital collaboration tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Future-Proof Mindset &amp; AI Literacy:</strong> A strong intrinsic interest in emerging technologies and a proactive mindset toward leveraging AI tools and their integration to automate routines, optimize workflows, and continuously elevate role efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working Style:</strong> Analytical yet empathetic mindset; highly structured &amp; solution-oriented working style; integrity champion &amp; confidentiality preserver, and exceptional communication skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluent in English (C1 level) and German (B1/B2) to confidently handle local as well as international legal cases and stakeholder collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Fuel for the Journey: Benefits to Support Your Ambitions</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Invest in Your Future</strong>: Regular feedback and our development program support your growth, helping you expand your skill set and achieve your career goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Easy Arrival to applike</strong>: From signing to settling in Hamburg, we’ve got you covered. Need a visa? No problem. Ready to build your new life and career at applike in Hamburg? We support every ambition - from learning German to a relocation bonus that helps you settle in and make Hamburg feel like home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Live Your Best Life, at Work and Beyond</strong>: We work in a hybrid setup with 3 core office days, plus flexible working hours. Enjoy 30 vacation days, 3 weeks of remote work per year, and free access to an in-house gym with lots of different fitness classes and mental health support through our Employee Assistance Program (EAP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Thrive Where You Work</strong>: Enjoy the Alster Lake view from our central office with top-notch equipment, fun open spaces, and a large variety of snacks and drinks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join the Community!</strong> Participate in regular team and company events, including hackathons and social gatherings. We work together, and we celebrate together, too.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Interview Process:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1st Interview with TA </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2nd Interview with Head of HR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case study</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case Study Presentation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meeting the Team and Managing Director</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to create an inspiring work environment for amazing people to achieve extraordinary things. <strong>Be part of it</strong>!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skip writing cover letters. Tell us about your most passionate personal project, your desired salary, and your earliest possible start date. We are looking forward to your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome applications from people who will contribute to the diversity of our company.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/applike-group/hr-partner-hamburg-492225","tags":["applike group"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792010418},{"slug":"engineering-intern-munich-206013","company_name":"Atira","title":"Engineering Intern","description":"<h2>About Atira</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Atira builds the commercial brain for industrials.</strong> Our agents 10x the sales engineers of today by offering the complete toolbox of tasks needed in complex environments. They handle everything from extracting and classifying requirements from incoming RFQs, orchestrating communication and information retrieval across multiple stakeholders and systems, while generating outcomes like documentation, production system inputs, or configuration recommendations. <strong>CRM. Atira. ERP.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the fastest growing teams in Munich and are looking for you to join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why engineers are the foundation of everything Atira ships</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Engineering Intern at Atira, you will work on frontier AI technology, such as (recursive) agent harnesses, runtimes, evals, inference and self-verification in complex engineering domains. You build the frameworks, primitives and scaffolding that let agents reliably handle complex industrial processes end to end, from the first inbound RFQ to the write-back into ERP.<br /><br />Misreading or wrongly interpreting a spec can cost a manufacturer six figures, so the challenges are real and the margin for error is thin.<br /><br />Where you trained matters less than what you've built and how clearly you can describe what broke. Atira is at a stage where you must own problems end to end, because what you ship today is what our customers use tomorrow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work on the agent runtime and harnesses.</strong> You improve the core components that let Atira's agents reason in complex engineering environments across the entire sales-engineering lifecycle, orchestrate themselves recursively at scale through dynamic programs, and handle arbitrarily large amounts of data. This includes the runtime/sandboxing, the harness, and the outer orchestration layer that ties it together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build out our AI moat.</strong> You are in charge of improving quality &amp; evals, improving the ontology layer that unlocks compounding process knowledge and fusing deterministic guardrails with agentic agency to make our agents actionable at enterprise level complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlock industrial scale.</strong> Industrials live in multi-modal, data-heavy environments: 1000-page inbounds, pricing lists, CAD files, ERP tables, legacy applications. You scale the AI systems behind them to millions of concurrent LLM requests in isolated sandboxes, with no silent failures, cost blowouts or latency explosions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Advance our internal tooling.</strong> FDEs, platform engineers and the GTM team depend on tooling you build to improve Atira's internal context layer, ambient agents, insight and observability engines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with FDEs when customer problems hit the platform.</strong> When an FDE hits a problem they should be able to pull you in. At a team of 20, the boundary between AI, platform and customer is thin, and you'll cross it regularly</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What we are looking for</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership, depth, and the instinct to take problems personally, go deep until you understand the system, and own the outcome including the parts that broke.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Your profile</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agent fluency sits on top of real engineering fundamentals. Solid skills in Python, TypeScript, or a comparable language. We value someone that can still code without AI. Ideally paired with hands-on experience with agents, evals, harnesses, runtimes, sandboxing and tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've gone further than most with AI-assisted development. Whether it's Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or your own setup, you've invested seriously in building the skills, context, and workflows to get maximum leverage from coding agents. This isn't a nice-to-have. We think engineers who have mastered this are fundamentally more productive, and we hire accordingly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You reason clearly about technical tradeoffs. You don’t need to have run systems at scale yet, but you can think through how a design would hold up at thousands of requests per second and explain the pros and cons of different approaches. Every design has tradeoffs: no free lunch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve demonstrated ownership and initiative. A side project you took further than anyone asked, a serious open-source contribution, a research project or a startup. We want evidence that you build without being told to and can explain what broke and why</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong technical foundation. Enrolled or recently graduated in Computer Science, Information Systems, AI, or a related technical field from a strong technical university (cracked dropouts can qualify too though)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full working proficiency in English. German is not required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're ready for a real internship, not a side gig. You can commit to at least three months full-time, on-site in Munich</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership: </strong>you'll be one of the early team members and shape both product and architecture as well as work closely with customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong peers and mentorship:</strong> work with and learn from engineers who have shipped AI systems in industrial environments at scale, with the opportunity for mentorship along the way</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impactful work: </strong>your code is deployed all across Europe’s and US industrial backbone, affecting how complex products and services are sold and configured worldwide</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> and additional benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Most importantly:</strong> Collaborate &amp; thrive in a high-performing but caring culture. We will own the industrial sales function but will do so with modesty and integrity</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What success looks like at the end of the internship</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've shipped meaningful improvements to the agent runtime, our AI pipelines and related systems that are running in production across multiple customer deployments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own one well-defined piece of our AI stack end to end (an eval suite, an internal tool, part of the context layer or the SDK), and the team trusts your judgment on how it should evolve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When something breaks in the part you own, you can trace it end to end, from agent behaviour back to the agent infrastructure layer, and fix it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve made an improvement to our internal AI tooling that the team now uses day to day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The design decisions in your piece have held up under real load, and you can explain the tradeoffs you made and what you’d do differently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If these metrics are met, we'd take you full-time without thinking twice</p></li></ul><p>Find <