al tactics, and follow-up strategies to drive consistent lead generation and engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and analyze the performance of field marketing campaigns and events, using data insights to refine strategies and deliver measurable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a detailed event calendar and actively identify new event opportunities that align with ClickHouse’s marketing goals and priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Give internal teams clear guidance on event responsibilities and task assignments, keeping them aligned with company goals.</p></li></ul><h2>What You Bring Along</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in field marketing, event marketing, or regional marketing within the B2B SaaS space. Experience in database or data analytics industries is required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success in driving pipeline generation and increasing brand awareness through field marketing efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent project management skills, with experience organizing and executing events at both small and large scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills, with the ability to measure and report on the effectiveness of marketing programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with sales teams to align on objectives, messaging, and campaign execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work independently in a fast-paced, remote-first environment, and comfort with ambiguity and evolving business needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">EMEA travel required more than 15% of the time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Field marketing experience in the UKI region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Account-based marketing experience building multi-channel regional campaigns that target key accounts, including