ftware Engineer embedded within a multifunctional team, you will collaborate with Product and Design counterparts in ideating, building and supporting the UI for <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> products and services, ensuring our merchants enjoy an optimal experience across all our frontend touchpoints.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We seek engineers who are versatile and enthusiastic about tackling new challenges across the full stack as we push technology forward. With your technical expertise, you will help define project priorities, manage deadlines, and ensure high-quality deliverables. You will be responsible for designing, developing, testing, deploying, maintaining, and enhancing software solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualifications</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficient in React and TypeScript: Able to implement and maintain features with limited guidance, following best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Modern software development practices, designing and architecting with security in mind</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good practical knowledge of OOP concepts and SOLID principles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of HTTP and RESTful design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Continuous Integration and Deployment workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Great communication skills and ability to interact effectively with multidisciplinary teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong customer focus with care for accessibility and User Experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building reliable, accessible and well-tested systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Desirable:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some experience with C# is nice to have</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of common security vulnerabilities and performance issues in web applications and knowing how to debug them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with asynchronous, event-driven architecture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Database experience with NoSQL, ElasticSearch or similar tool</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/front-end-engineer-london-230080","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792021221},{"slug":"head-of-legal-england-23879","company_name":"Onhires","title":"Head of Legal","description":"<h2>Remote | United Kingdom | Crypto &amp; Payments | FCA Authorisation | Employment or B2B</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our client is an established, profitable fintech operating at the intersection of crypto and traditional payments. It runs a consumer on/off-ramp platform and a fast-growing B2B infrastructure business: APIs and white-label solutions that let exchanges, neobanks, PSPs, wallets and other platforms embed regulated crypto and fiat services. The company is authorised under MiCA and PSD2 in the EU and is now building its regulatory presence in the UK. The culture is owner-led, high-ownership and low-bureaucracy: decisions are made quickly and close to the founders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior, hands-on legal role with a single, clear mandate: own the company’s UK regulatory build. You will report directly to the CEO and be the most senior legal voice in the business on UK matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The UK’s new cryptoasset regime takes effect in October 2027. From that date, regulated cryptoasset activity in the UK requires FCA authorisation. You will own a first-wave authorisation under this new regime end to end, alongside a UK e-money application. For a regulatory lawyer, this is a career-defining piece of work, and the window to start it is narrow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role has no direct reports at hire. You will work closely with the company’s EU legal function. This is a deliberately focused UK mandate, not a group legal role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>FCA cryptoasset authorisation:</strong> perimeter analysis of B2C and B2B activities against the new regime, application strategy, drafting, regulatory business plan input, RFI handling and dialogue through to decision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UK EMI application:</strong> ownership on the same basis, including sequencing between the two applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>FCA relationship:</strong> acting as the senior in-house legal counterpart to the regulator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UK conduct perimeter:</strong> the cryptoasset financial promotions regime, Consumer Duty, the UK Travel Rule, and safeguarding and prudential requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Post-authorisation readiness:</strong> governance, senior manager and certification considerations, reporting and disclosures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>External counsel:</strong> briefing, directing and quality-controlling UK external counsel, and managing that spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International expansion:</strong> legal lead on additional licence applications in other jurisdictions, and advice where the UK and EU regulatory perimeters meet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial legal:</strong> drafting and negotiating English-law B2B agreements. This includes MSAs, API and white-label terms, referral and agent agreements, and banking, payment and card scheme counterparty agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UK consumer-facing legal:</strong> consumer terms, financial promotions review and UK-specific disclosures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UK employment:</strong> UK employment law and contractor arrangements, in partnership with HR.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we are looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified solicitor or barrister in England &amp; Wales, typically with 8+ years PQE.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on UK financial services regulatory experience, including at least one FCA authorisation or variation of permission that you personally owned or materially led, from perimeter analysis to decision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct, personal interaction with the FCA: correspondence, meetings and representation that you led yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Crypto or digital-asset legal experience at licensed or established firms, such as registered or authorised exchanges, regulated on/off-ramps, licensed custodians or infrastructure providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cryptoasset, e-money or payments perimeter experience. Engagement with the 2025–26 FCA cryptoasset consultations is highly relevant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to draft and negotiate English-law B2B fintech agreements independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning regulatory outcomes, not only advising on them. Law-firm backgrounds are welcome where this is evident.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to take a clear position under pressure from senior stakeholders and counterparties, and to translate legal risk into business options with a recommendation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating as a remote senior with no legal support structure beneath you, working with a leadership team based outside the UK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical use of AI tools in legal drafting, research or review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent legal English to regulator-facing standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing right to work in the UK, and the ability to attend regulator meetings in London as required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team management experience is not required. We welcome strong senior counsel ready to step into a Head of Legal role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous Head of Legal, GC or senior counsel role at a UK-authorised EMI, PI or FCA-registered cryptoasset firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of a firm moving from AML registration to full FSMA authorisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Involvement in industry working groups or trade association engagement on the new UK crypto regime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">SM&amp;CR experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of UK safeguarding and prudential requirements for e-money and payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Crown Dependency (Jersey, Guernsey, Isle of Man) or Australian regulatory exposure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Card scheme legal experience, such as Visa/Mastercard rules and principal membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building a legal or regulatory function in a jurisdiction from scratch.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s on offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A direct reporting line to the CEO and ownership of the company’s UK market entry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A defining role in a first-wave authorisation under the UK’s new cryptoasset regime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A remote setup in the UK, with a flat structure and fast decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employment or B2B contract, with a performance bonus linked to UK authorisation milestones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast, transparent hiring process, typically completed within four weeks.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/onhires/head-of-legal-england-23879","tags":["Administrative & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"England","created_at":1792021220},{"slug":"remote-senior-finance-systems-accountant-103614","company_name":"Oviva","title":"Senior Finance Systems Accountant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Oviva?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Oviva, we’re on a mission to make sustainable, personalized, clinically effective care accessible to everyone as we build Europe’s leading AI-powered chronic care platform. Our digital programmes help people manage weight-related illnesses by focusing on what matters most: improving health, building confidence, and enhancing quality of life.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, we have supported over one million people across the UK, Switzerland, and Germany. Our mission is powered by a dedicated team operating across four countries, including our hub in Poland. Every conversation, coaching session, and line of code brings us closer to a healthier future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our journey is accelerating: In 2026, we secured €200 million in Series D funding led by Kinnevik and a group of leading global investors. This investment fuels our next phase of growth, allowing us to scale our AI-enabled chronic care platform across Europe and expand our support to even more people living with chronic conditions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us, and be part of the team making that future possible!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Senior Finance Systems Accountant, you’ll own how we plan and report day to day, turning data into systems people trust. You’ll work across Finance, BI, Engineering and Product to make things simpler, smarter and more automated, from a fully remote UK base. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be joining a newly formed, growing Finance Systems team, alongside our wider finance function. Every day looks a little different here, and we value people who spot opportunities and act on them. This is a rare, exciting chance to shape finance systems through a period of real transformation, with genuine room to grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own Pigment</strong> day to day, from user access and models to workflows, dashboards and controls. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead enhancements </strong>from first idea through testing, release and user adoption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reconcile Pigment</strong> with our ERP and other data sources, track down differences and fix them at source.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Train and support users</strong>, and document the processes that keep data flowing and issues visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with the Finance Systems Director </strong>to improve our wider systems, including the ERP, integrations and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Spot opportunities to simplify work</strong> through better processes, automation and responsible use of AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Translate</strong> between technical and finance teams, so everyone is fully aligned.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on Pigment experience:</strong> in administration, modelling and reporting, and the confidence to diagnose and improve models independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finance background: </strong>Experience as a systems accountant or in a similar finance systems role, with solid accounting and controls knowledge; as well as experience across FP&amp;A, financial reporting or management reporting. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A detective’s eye for data</strong>: you can trace it across systems, reconcile and explain. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and good judgement</strong>: ability to juggle competing priorities and see work through to the end. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication skills: </strong>Ability to tailor the message to technical, finance and non-finance colleagues alike. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems improvement: </strong>A track record of turning business requirements into working system changes, tested and adopted by users. A continuous improvement mindset, with the confidence to challenge the status quo and a real interest in automation and AI.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Having a culture that people want to work in, is very important to us. We do this by keeping our values at the forefront of everything we do:<br />We put the patient first. We empower our teams. We make it happen<br /><br />Oviva is passionate about creating an inclusive culture that celebrates diverse voices and perspectives. We are proud to be a Disability Confident Employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and identities.<br /><br />Ready to help shape the future of digital healthcare? Apply today!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-JN1 </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/oviva/remote-senior-finance-systems-accountant-103614","tags":["Finance & BI"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote UK","created_at":1792021219},{"slug":"product-designer-london-496474","company_name":"Getscope","title":"Product Designer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getscope.ai/"><u>Scope</u></a> automates the data collection that's slowing down the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standards are vital for the safety of our infrastructure. Spending hours manually documenting them is not.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dave is an inspector. Today he's climbing through one of Europe's biggest chemical plants, looking for the corrosion that could shut the whole site down, with a notebook and pen in hand. Tomorrow, he'll spend even longer on the part of the job he hates: turning those scribbles into a report.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building the best AI-native data collection layer for the 2 billion field workers like Dave. Scope radically simplifies how inspectors collect data in the field, make decisions, and produce reports. Along the way, we're building the world's largest dataset on the condition of the built world and the decisions experts make about it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It's a $2T market and we're just getting started, with ambitions. We work with 6 of the top 10 companies in the space. Our customers inspect facilities and products for companies including AstraZeneca and SpaceX.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've assembled a best-in-class team: acquired and future founders, people from institutions like Imperial, Carnegie Mellon and Oxford, and from firms like Goldman Sachs, Flexport and Amazon.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since launching from Entrepreneurs First in 2024, we've raised an oversubscribed $20m round led by<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.indexventures.com/"> <u>Index Ventures</u></a>, the firm behind Figma, Revolut and Wiz, with 100+ unicorns backed to date.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring our first Product Designer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every engineer at Scope is a product engineer: they talk to users, decide what to build and ship it themselves. You'll work the same way, with design as your edge, and help the engineers around you to build a better product. That covers the whole experience, not just the surface: which problem we solve, how the flow works, what happens when things go wrong, and how it all looks. You'll work closely with the engineers, with Ish our Product Manager, and with Jakob the CTO.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work in person five days a week from our office in Farringdon.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll work on</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some examples of surfaces in our product that will need your help:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mobile app gets used inside tanks and on top of pressure vessels. People wear thick gloves, there's usually no signal, and one hand is often holding on to something. Most of what makes a normal app pleasant doesn't apply there, so a big part of the job is figuring out what does.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Then there's the report. How AI and the inspector will work together to produce 40 page reports and review them is something nobody has designed well yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inspectors but also decision makers should be able to ask things like "Which tanks were over the corrosion limit last year?". Sometimes the right interface will be a chat but often it isn't.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go on site with inspectors and test your designs there, gloves and all.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the design of every launch, down to the empty states.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype fast, in code when it helps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work next to engineers while they build, so the details come out right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide with Ish and Jakob which problems are worth solving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the design system that lets engineers ship great work without waiting on you.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 3 years designing products that were shipped.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that shows the messy middle, not just the final screens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You sweat the mobile details: touch targets, offline, errors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have opinions on where AI helps and where it gets in the way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd happily put on a hard hat to understand a problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus if you've designed for industrial or field work, or prototype in code.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio deep dive with Ish and an engineer: one project, including what went wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with a cofounder: Jonny (CEO) or Jakob (CTO and CPO).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onsite: a real Scope design problem, worked on with the team, then a short presentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer!</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">£70k to £100k base + significant equity, so you have a stake in what you are building</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full visa sponsorship, giving us access to global talent and an international, diverse team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tools to do your job, including a brand new MacBook and Scope merch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous above-market annual leave allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bupa private medical (0 excess, pre-existing conditions covered) + Bupa dental</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee pension through NEST</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible parental leave (including adoption leave)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy meal-prep lunch and dinners, a fully stocked fridge, and team lunches on Fridays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular events including off-sites</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We value diverse perspectives. If you don't match every point above but this is the kind of problem you want to work on, we strongly encourage you to apply.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/getscope/product-designer-london-496474","tags":["Engineering and Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792021219},{"slug":"senior-integrated-operations-engineer-team-y-london-225954","company_name":"Rocket Lab Corporation","title":"Senior Integrated Operations Engineer - Team Y","description":"<div class="content-intro"><p><strong>ABOUT ROCKET LAB</strong></p>
