king hand-in-hand with Research Scientists, you'll make every GPU count.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral AI is hiring an expert in pushing large language model's GPU utilization and performance to their limits.. In this role, you will own the performance of our models end-to-end: writing the low-level code that extracts the maximum capacity from high-end hardware, and rethinking model architectures so they run efficiently at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop <strong>low-level code</strong> that takes full advantage of high-end GPUs and <strong>maxes out their capacity</strong> — from custom kernels to memory-layout and communication optimisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rethink parts of the generative model architecture</strong> to make them more suitable for efficient inference, in collaboration with Research Scientists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integrate low-level efficient code into a high-level MLOps framework</strong>, so that optimisations benefit every training run and deployment rather than a single experiment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile, benchmark and squeeze performance out of large-scale training and inference on thousands of GPUs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model LLM execution on various GPUs with high fidelity to assess hardware usage and build serving performance estimates.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High technical competence for writing custom low-level kernels</strong> and pushing GPUs to their limits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High expertise in the distributed computation infrastructure</strong> of current-generation GPU clusters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Overall understanding of the field of generat