&lt;li&gt;Stratégie et relation client&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stratégie &amp;amp; Déploiement :&lt;/strong&gt; Concevoir, piloter et exécuter les stratégies de campagnes d&#39;Influence et de Social Media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conseil stratégique :&lt;/strong&gt; Apporter un conseil proactif et structuré aux clients sur leurs enjeux de réputation digitale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rédaction &amp;amp; Contenus :&lt;/strong&gt; Rédiger des recommandations stratégiques, plans annuels, pitchs, recommandations d&#39;influenceurs, briefs créatifs, éléments de langage/Q&amp;amp;A, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relations Médias &amp;amp; Influence :&lt;/strong&gt; Mener et orienter les actions de partenariat, de portage et d&#39;engagement auprès des créateurs de contenu, influenceurs clés, médias et leaders d&#39;opinion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gestion des opportunités et risques :&lt;/strong&gt; Identifier proactivement les opportunités de développement de compte ainsi que les risques potentiels, et réagir avec rapidité et pertinence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Insights :&lt;/strong&gt; Exploiter les données, analytics social media et insights d&#39;audience pour optimiser la performance des campagnes et étayer vos recommandations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développement et pilotage commercial&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance financière :&lt;/strong&gt; Assurer le suivi des indicateurs financiers (rentabilité, marge, suivi budgétaire, gestion des dépassements d&#39;honoraires et encours) de vos dossiers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Développement commercial :&lt;/strong&gt; Détecter les opportunités de croissance chez les clients existants et participer activement à l&#39;élaboration de propositions commerciales pour de nouveaux prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pilotage budgétaire :&lt;/strong&gt; Élaborer et gérer avec précision des budgets de campagnes complexes (honoraires, budgets d&#39;influence, production).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Présentation :&lt;/strong&gt; Démontrer une excellente aisance à l&#39;oral pour présenter et valoriser l&#39;ensemble des expertises et services de l&#39;agence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Profil recherché : Ce dont vous avez besoin pour réussir&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience :&lt;/strong&gt; 6 à 8 ans d&#39;expérience en agence PR / Influence / Social Media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise métier :&lt;/strong&gt; Maîtrise approfondie des écosystèmes d&#39;influence, des réseaux sociaux, des relations publics et des stratégies de contenu. Vous appréciez tout autant les sujets corporate que les lancements de produits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise sectorielle&amp;nbsp;: &lt;/strong&gt;la connaissance du secteur de la santé est un plus.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relation client :&lt;/strong&gt; Capacités relationnelles et de gestion de compte&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences analytiques &amp;amp; financières &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership :&lt;/strong&gt; Capacités d&#39;écoute, d&#39;encadrement et de transmission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce Que Nous Vous Offrons :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Un environnement stimulant :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Intégrez une agence reconnue mondialement, au cœur des stratégies de communication des plus grandes marques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Un encadrement de qualité :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Vous serez accompagné(e) par des experts passionnés qui vous transmettront leur savoir-faire, avec des points réguliers et un feedback constructif pour vous aider à progresser.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une expérience professionnalisante :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Développez des compétences clés et construisez une carrière solide dans un secteur en constante évolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une culture d’entreprise forte :&lt;/strong&gt; Rejoignez une équipe dynamique et collaborative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Des avantages attractifs :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Télétravail possible (2 jours/semaine).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forfait mobilité mensuel de 45,40 euros (carte Swile) pour transports publics ou mobilités durables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Accès à nos deux restaurants d’entreprise du Campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;14 jours de RTT par an&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Accès aux avantages du Comité d’Entreprise (cinéma, chèques cadeaux, remboursements sportifs…).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Votre place est chez Burson :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre vision est de faire de Burson la référence en matière de formation pour les professionnels de la communication créative et les leaders de demain. Nous offrons un environnement de travail stimulant où les collaborateurs motivés et ambitieux peuvent développer leurs compétences, étendre leur réseau et élaborer des stratégies innovantes pour les plus grandes marques. Notre engagement envers le développement de nos talents se traduit par des opportunités de formation, des programmes de mentorat avec des leaders du secteur, et une culture d&#39;entreprise stimulante et inclusive qui encourage la collaboration et l&#39;innovation. Nous avons également mis en place des programmes de reconnaissance et de fidélisation pour nos meilleurs talents. Nous investissons dans nos collaborateurs car nous sommes convaincus que leur réussite est aussi la nôtre.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Burson, nous sommes une agence d&#39;apprenants permanents. Nous savons que l&#39;excellence en créativité et en communication exige une compréhension fine et nuancée. C&#39;est pourquoi nous recherchons des collaborateurs talentueux de tous horizons et de toutes cultures. Ces talents sont essentiels pour concevoir des idées audacieuses, favoriser un dialogue constructif, créer des expériences enrichissantes et stimuler l&#39;innovation pour nos clients. Votre point de vue unique, votre talent, fait de vous une #BursonPerson.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En cliquant sur « Soumettre la candidature », vous nous transmettez les informations saisies. Avant de le faire, veuillez consulter notre politique de confidentialité en matière &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;de recrutement. &lt;/a&gt;Les candidats résidant &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;en Californie. &lt;/a&gt;sont invités à consulter notre politique de confidentialité californienne pour le recrutement. Ce document détaille l&#39;utilisation de vos données personnelles lors de votre candidature et explique comment les mettre à jour ou les supprimer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong at Burson:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is for Burson to be the leading ‘academy company’ for creative communications professionals and emerging leaders. We provide a dynamic environment where ambitious colleagues come to elevate their skills, expand their networks, and ultimately, produce the best solutions for today’s leading brands. Our commitment to your growth is reflected in our robust benefits and people programs, which include professional development opportunities, mentorship programs with industry leaders, a vibrant and inclusive company culture fostering collaboration and innovation and packages designed to reward and retain top talent. We invest in our people because we believe their success is our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Burson, we’re an agency of learn-it-alls. We recognize that the things we do best, creativity and communications, require a level of nuanced understanding. That’s why it’s imperative for us to hire extraordinarily talented people of all backgrounds and identities. Without that we can’t do the essential work of inspiring bold ideas, fostering constructive dialogue, cultivating meaningful experiences, and driving innovation and creativity for our partners. Your unique point of view—your talent—is what makes you a #BursonPerson, and it’s how we deliver exceptional results for our clients, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click the &quot;Submit Application&quot; button below, this will send any information you add below to Burson. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy. &lt;/a&gt;California residents should read our  &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice. &lt;/a&gt;This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/bursonglobalcareers/account-director-social-media-influence-f-h-paris-paris-8157","tags":["Burson"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, Paris","created_at":1792011343},{"slug":"cdd-brand-communication-senior-manager-paris-paris-407951","company_name":"hellofresh","title":"CDD - Brand & Communication Senior Manager - (M/F/X)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position for 8 months to cover maternity leave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Brand &amp;amp; Communication Senior Manager, you will be responsible for implementing the Demand Generation communication strategy and roadmap. You will own the conception and supervise the development of communication activities, including brand campaigns (online and offline), social media activities, PR &amp;amp; events, focusing on increasing the efficiency of the campaigns and making sure it perfectly reflects the brand positioning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will focus on creating impactful and creative campaigns, working closely with both local and global resources, and analyse and report the performance of these activities on a regular basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage different stakeholders at a local level, including a Junior communication manager and a Copywriter, as well as the different agencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will coordinate with different local marketing teams to perfectly operate the plan, like the Influencer team or the Online Paid team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be in regular contact with international stakeholders to align on the implementation of the campaigns, share best practices and gather useful consumer insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a Management position. It requires strong management skills, as well as strong project management and coordination skills, due to the broad nature of the projects. You will work hand in hand with the Brand &amp;amp; Communication Director, being her direct report.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner of the development of Demand Generation brand activities, including brand campaigns (online and offline), chef partnership, social media and PR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the conception, planning, production and report of the brand activities, liaising with a wide range of stakeholders (including the Global Brand Team, Agencies, Local marketing teams) and ensuring that we deliver a quality result on time and on budget. Brand activities include a broad nature of projects such as video campaigns, offline campaigns, brand partnership campaigns, organic social media, stunts…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse campaign performance and channel results; generate actionable insights and optimisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the main point of contact for other local teams, working together on on-brand communications for all touchpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage our local Brand Campaign Manager and Copywriter, as well as drive the Creative Agency and Social Media agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years experience in communication/brand project management in a B2C scale up/eCommerce brand or top communication agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand mindset: you are passionate about brands, creative advertising and marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset: you analyse the performance of your work and generate actionable learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset: you like working with different stakeholders, with a solution-driven attitude,&amp;nbsp; with strong people and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage different projects, with efficient processes, respect of deadlines and budget conscience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous, organised, proactive and adaptable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and French - both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you get?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dynamic, international environment with a strong company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A supportive, passionate, proactive and dynamic French team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offices in the heart of Paris, in the 1st arrondissement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid setup combining remote work and time in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perks: HelloFresh discounts, Swile meal vouchers, Gymlib access, transport benefits, and everything else that makes coming to the office great&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our recruitment process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ll review your profile. If it&#39;s a match, we&#39;ll invite you to a series of interviews and a case study. We&#39;re committed to scheduling interviews quickly so we can welcome you to HelloFresh as soon as possible!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your start at HelloFresh:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you join, we&#39;ll cook up onboarding sessions that let you meet every manager and get a real feel for how HelloFresh works. You&#39;ll also have time to get to know your team better before diving into your responsibilities!&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/hellofresh/cdd-brand-communication-senior-manager-paris-paris-407951","tags":["Brand Marketing"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, Paris","created_at":1792011338},{"slug":"customer-care-specialist-paris-336480","company_name":"Lucis","title":"Customer Care Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Making preventive health the default for every human in Europe</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lucis.life/?utm_source=career_job_desc&amp;utm_medium=content">Lucis</a>, we believe healthcare should be preventive, not reactive. We’re building the OS for human longevity to help people add more healthy years to their lives. You can read more about who we are and how we work <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lucis.life/careers?utm_source=career_job_desc&amp;utm_medium=content">here</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health is complex, personal, and deeply important to our members. As the voice of Lucis clients, you support them throughout their health journey and own member happiness end to end.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With rapid member growth, we are hiring our first dedicated <strong>Customer Care Team Lead</strong>. You will own the member experience end-to-end, stabilize our operational metrics, and build and manage a world-class support team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Member support:</strong> Resolve member and lab partner inquiries via chat, email and phone, with warmth, precision and a sense of urgency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Phone-first when it matters:</strong> Pick up the phone whenever a situation calls for a human voice: a delayed result, a stressful moment, a confused member.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Know your boundaries:</strong> Work hand in hand with our medical team and know exactly when to escalate a health question rather than answer it yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Voice of the member:</strong> Spot recurring issues and turn them into clear, structured feedback for the product and ops teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contribute to projects:</strong> Take part in initiatives that improve the member experience, like rebuilding our Help Center, designing proactive care for lab delays, or automating repetitive workflows with AI.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re passionate about the future of human health and want your work to help people stay healthy for longer. You move quickly from idea to execution, take full ownership of what you build, and work best with talented people who care as much as you do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive in fast‑moving environments, learn by doing, and value feedback as a way to continuously improve. You use AI the way others use a calculator: naturally, to go faster and think bigger.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>You’ll fit in well if</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 1+ years in B2C customer care, support, hospitality, or any role where you dealt directly with customers. Strong recent graduates with relevant experience are welcome too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bilingual:</strong> Fluent in both English and French, written and spoken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People-first energy:</strong> You bring genuine warmth and empathy to every interaction, and you turn routine support into memorable experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rigorous precision:</strong> Exceptional attention to detail, with zero tolerance for misquotes, wrong information or operational errors. In health, accuracy is care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder mindset:</strong> When something breaks twice, your instinct is to fix the root cause, not just the ticket.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support tooling:</strong> You've used Intercom or similar support tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI automation:</strong> You've already used AI tools to automate part of your work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup mindset:</strong> You thrive in early-stage environments with high autonomy, rapid execution and clear communication.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call, culture &amp; role fit (20 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case study interview (30-60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep dive and team chat, on-site (2 hours)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference calls</p></li></ul><h2></h2><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together from our Paris hub. We’re passionate about what we’re building and believe the fastest way to create something exceptional is side by side. We’re open to relocation support for the right individuals, and we welcome missionaries who travel to work with us in Paris on a regular basis.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rigor without ego:</strong> Audits, science, and code all deserve the same high bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Radical ownership:</strong> Feedback loops are short; everyone contributes to building the best version of Lucis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Velocity over perfection:</strong> We ship daily and prefer a good decision today over a perfect one next week.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lucis/customer-care-specialist-paris-336480","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792010419},{"slug":"head-of-security-paris-278556","company_name":"Morpho","title":"Head of Security","description":"<h2>About Morpho</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Morpho is a leading Decentralized Finance (DeFi) lending protocol backed by a16z crypto, Paradigm, Ribbit Capital, Apollo, Vaneck, Coinbase Ventures, Variant and 50 others to build an open credit network giving anyone, anywhere, access to the best possible terms. Morpho is experiencing exponential adoption, with over billion in deposits on the network and used by institutional clients including Bitwise, Galaxy, and Anchorage Digital and the largest crypto exchanges, such as Coinbase, Binance, and Kraken. Now, Morpho is scaling its team of contributors to establish itself as the open credit network, not just of DeFi, but of the world.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Why Morpho Exists</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone has the potential to build something great for the world. But fulfilling that ambition almost always requires more: people willing to trust you with their capital. Yet access to capital still depends on where you live, who you know, and which institutions are willing to trust you. Even when capital is available, it sits fragmented across disconnected networks and hidden behind intermediaries. The result is a system that fails most of the people it should serve. Borrowers overpay. Lenders earn less than they should. Many are shut out entirely, not because they are unworthy of credit, but because today's infrastructure was never built to connect them. Morpho exists to solve this. Full article <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://morpho.org/blog/why-morpho-exists/">here</a>.</p><h2>Location:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paris or remote (from -5h GMT up to +2h GMT to ensure sufficient overlap with the rest of the team).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Head of Security, you'll define and drive Morpho's security strategy across the entire organization - corporate IT, cloud and infrastructure, application, supply chain, identity, incident response, threat intelligence, and counterparty security - and you'll build the team and function to deliver it. This is a hands-on leadership role: in the early days you'll personally do the work while you hire, and you'll stay close enough to the technical detail to earn the trust of a deeply technical organization. You'll also be Morpho's credible security voice, internally to leadership, and externally to the integrators, institutions, and ecosystem partners who depend on us. You'll partner closely with Engineering on infrastructure and deployment integrity, and with our Integration team, which works with various partners across the Morpho ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Responsibilities:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and continuously evolve Morpho's security strategy and roadmap across, cloud/infrastructure, application, supply-chain, identity, and operational security.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the security function - hire, grow, and develop the team, recruiting skillsets across security operations and application security.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversight of the IT function</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay hands-on. Personally execute critical security work - threat modeling, architecture review, control implementation, and incident command - while the team scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the governance architecture: a coherent security framework that ties tooling and controls together, rather than accumulating tools in isolation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own incident response end to end - runbooks, incident command, severity and escalation structure, and market communication during an event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run a counterparty security program for curators and partners - identity verification, screening, operational diligence, and bidirectional incident-coordination channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Morpho's certification strategy (e.g. SOC 2, ISO 27001), meeting both the spirit and the letter sustainably.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Morpho's security posture externally - to fintechs, financial institutions, and the broader ecosystem - and internally to executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner cross-functionally with Engineering, Protocol, and Integrations, driving security outcomes through both direct ownership and influence.</p></li></ul><h2>What Success Looks Like:</h2><h3>First 30 Days</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built a clear, independent picture of Morpho's posture, architecture, threat model, and in-flight work - and pressure-tested the existing strategy against it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've met the team and established working relationships with the people who own the surfaces you'll most depend on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the path-to-funds attack surface in depth and have an early, evidence-based view of the highest-severity risks and quick wins.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know exactly where incident-response readiness stands today.</p></li></ul><h3>First 60 Days</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've published a clearly prioritized security roadmap with clear sequencing, owners, and the rationale for what's deferred and aligned leadership behind it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've defined the team build-out plan and opened the first hire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're personally driving the top-severity gaps - identity and authentication enforcement, deployment guardrails, and a documented incident-response runbook among them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've set the governance framework and the certification path in motion.</p></li></ul><h3>First 90 Days</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable progress closing the highest-priority gaps, with key controls enforced rather than optional.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A documented incident-response capability that's been validated by at least one tabletop exercise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring underway, and a clear operating rhythm established with Engineering, Protocol, and Integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Morpho's external security posture is taking shape - trust surface, counterparty security program, and ecosystem engagement - and you're recognized internally and externally as Morpho's credible security voice.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Must-have Experience &amp; Skills:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in security, several of them building or leading a security function, ideally at a crypto/web3, fintech, or financial-services company where security is core to the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong grasp of the crypto/web3 threat model</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building and growing a security team from a small base, recruiting across security operations and application/infrastructure security.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep, hands-on technical expertise across cloud, infrastructure, CI/CD, supply-chain, identity, and application security - you do the work, not just direct it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owned incident response end to end, including incident command and external communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp prioritization and the ability to galvanize action through hard and soft influence, including driving outcomes through teams you don't own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional, organized, responsive communication - credible to executives and to external audiences from fintechs to Fortune 500 institutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humble.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An established network and public profile in the security or crypto-security community, and comfort representing security work publicly (talks, writing, framework contribution).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offensive security depth, or experience standing up red/blue capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with institutional and regulatory expectations and threat-sharing networks (e.g. Crypto ISAC, TIBER-style frameworks).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taken an organization through certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent)</p></li></ul><h2>Perks &amp; Benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We design benefits around deep work and growth, so you can do the best work of your career. Expect fair, top-tier compensation, real flexibility, time together in Paris, great health coverage, and support to keep learning.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and hire based on talent, potential, and values alignment.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/morpho/head-of-security-paris-278556","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792010419},{"slug":"finance-manager-financial-control-accounting-paris-338350","company_name":"Joko","title":"Finance Manager, Financial Control & Accounting","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Joko, our mission is to we help consumers save time and money when shopping online or in-store. <br /><br />Founded in Paris, Joko is a tech company and certified B Corp with over 120 talents across Paris, Barcelona, and New York (and beyond). More than 7 million users already save money every day at 10,000+ merchants with Joko. <br /><br />From cashback and automatic coupons to price alerts, we've kept expanding our products to make shopping smarter. Today, Joko is an AI shopping app: with Juno, our shopping assistant, users can find the right product at the best price in only a few seconds, with recommendations that get sharper the more they use it.<br /><br />Having reached profitability in our core market, we’re now scaling globally, with a strong focus on the US. <br /><br /><strong>It’s still day 1, come build the future of shopping with us!</strong></p><h3><strong>💰 Our Finance team</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Finance team ensures Joko's financial health and long-term success. We manage everything from financial planning and accounting to financing and cash management.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We make sure every euro is put to its best use, working closely with all teams, we provide the insights and structure needed to scale efficiently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we scale, we're splitting Finance into three specialized poles: <strong>FP&amp;A</strong>, <strong>Finance Operations (Financial Control &amp; Accounting)</strong>, and <strong>Procurement</strong>. This role anchors <strong>Finance Operations (Financial Control &amp; Accounting)</strong> — the pole that keeps Joko's financial information accurate, timely, and audit-ready. You'll report directly to <strong>Quentin, our COO</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>✨ Why this role is special</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Finance Operations (Financial Control &amp; Accounting) is a brand-new specialized pole at Joko — previously bundled into a single generalist Finance Manager role. You'll be the first person to own this scope end to end, with direct visibility to the COO and VP Finance with real influence over how the function is built as the company scales past 200 people across multiple geographies.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You set the standards, not just follow them:</strong> as the pole's first hire, the processes, controls, and calendar you establish now become the backbone the rest of Finance builds on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A true partner in automation:</strong> you'll work hand-in-hand with a dedicated BizOps partner to automate what can be automated — this isn't a role where you're expected to grind through manual work alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International scope from day one:</strong> France, the US, and future markets — you'll help build the multi-entity, multi-country accounting backbone as Joko expands.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>🎯 What you will do</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Finance Manager, Finance Operations (Financial Control &amp; Accounting)</strong>, your main mission is to own the reliability, timeliness, and completeness of Joko's financial information. Rather than doing the bookkeeping — we have an external accounting partner for that — you set the standards, drive the calendar, and hold your internal and external stakeholders accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities will include:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive the closing calendar:</strong> own the monthly and annual closing calendar, holding our external accounting partner and auditors to a high standard;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own our legal reporting package:</strong> make sure the P&amp;L, balance sheet, and cash flow statement are always accurate and delivered on time;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Oversee AP/AR end to end:</strong> keep invoicing, payment runs, and collections under control;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead our international accounting build-out:</strong> as we open new entities and markets, including our IFRS consolidation framework;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own cash management:</strong> reconciliation, yield optimization, and day-to-day treasury;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the main point of contact for our banking and accounting partners</strong>, and a key interface for auditors as we scale toward IPO readiness;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuously strengthen and document our financial processes and controls</strong>, working hand-in-hand with a dedicated BizOps partner to automate what can be automated, making everything more robust and less error-prone as the company scales.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>👀 Who we're looking for</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 4–8 years, with a strong foundation in accounting or audit (Big 4 or equivalent), ideally combined with in-house experience in a scale-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> A master's degree from a top business school. A double degree in accounting (DCG/DSCG) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial rigor:</strong> Deep understanding of French GAAP and treasury fundamentals — you bring the same discipline to a closing cycle as you do to a cash position.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International mindset:</strong> Excited to build a multi-entity, multi-country accounting backbone as we expand; IFRS exposure is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder management:</strong> You build trust with partners inside and outside Joko, and you're comfortable holding them accountable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Problem solving:</strong> You dig into the root cause and fix things.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI centricity:</strong> You use AI in your daily work today, and you're excited to help automate reporting and reconciliation as part of Joko's AI-first finance ambition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluent French and English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>💎 Our perks</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>(Some of the benefits listed below are available to full-time positions only)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Joko, we believe that flexibility and trust are essential. Our work environment reflects this through:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible remote</strong> : If you live in Paris, you can choose to work from our office or from home with no constraints. If you live elsewhere, we can provide access to a coworking space and a coworking budget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work from anywhere</strong> : Want to spend a month in Italy while working? You can work from most countries in the world for up to 3 months per year.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">On top of that, we offer plenty of perks:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💸 Top-market compensation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Equity for everyone with the chance to own a piece of what you build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤖 Half-day each week dedicated to leveling up with AI by exploring new tools, iterating hard, and sharpening your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 Yearly offsite in amazing locations and budget for team-building events &amp; monthly in-person gatherings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💪 Contribution to your ClassPass subscription</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍼 8-week leave paid 100% for the second parent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">…and much more, check the full list <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://notion.so/joko/20f4ead2bfc54137b9d805bd9abbb758?pvs=4&amp;v=e2baac50c1844149a219895e0d1c2912"><strong>here</strong></a>!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🤝 Our hiring process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro call:</strong> Quick screening with the Hiring Manager or the Talent team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 1 – Team interview (45 min):</strong> Conversation with two Joko team members (could include the Hiring Manager, people from the team you’d join, or colleagues from other teams).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 2 – Role-specific assessments</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>For non-engineering roles</strong>: A take-home case study followed by a 45-min interview. We assess both your output