edge Sharing Sessions. In addition, each young graduate will be accompanied by a dedicated wingmate/mentor who will guide and help them build their technical growth vision.</p><p><br>As a young graduate you will join a team of Data Scientists, Data Engineers and Cloud Engineers who work hand-in-hand with our customers on designing and implementing their industry-specific use cases. You will be directly involved in discussing the client’s challenges and needs and will have chances to develop your client-facing skills. You will be responsible for developing, deploying, and automating our AI services and cloud infrastructure. You will also learn to carefully analyse a given problem and apply the relevant tools and techniques to solve it.<br></p><p><strong>In general you will:</strong></p><ul><li>use software best practices in continuous integration and delivery, versioning and automation;</li><li>use your skills to build and maintain service and data infrastructure;</li><li>participate as junior engineer in all phases of the software development life cycle - planning, implementation, deployment, testing and maintenance;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Are You the team member we are looking for?</strong></p><p>In order to be successful in this role, you are/have:</p><ul><li>motivated and eager to learn different aspects of engineering</li><li>comfortable interacting with technical and business people</li><li>strong communication and presentation skills</li><li>recently graduated/finishing your MSc or BSc in Computer Science or related major;</li><li>familiar with version control and collaboration tooling (git)</li><li>familiar with CI/CD frameworks and automated deployment concepts (i.e Docker, K8s)</li><li>fluent in both <strong>English</strong> and <strong>German</strong></li><li>available for a minimum of 32h a week.</li><li><strong>ready to start on the 1st of February </strong></li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul><li>Exposur