d where your experience can directly contribute to how we mature our project management approach.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Lead multidisciplinary projects from initiation through delivery, ensuring they are delivered on time, within scope and within budget.</p></li><li><p>Act as the main point of contact for customers, partners and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Manage projects related to offshore, subsea or marine operations, such as subsea cable installation, geotechnical monitoring, marine surveys or similar activities.</p></li><li><p>Coordinate closely with R&amp;D, engineering, production, commercial and other internal teams to ensure successful project execution.</p></li><li><p>Translate technical requirements into clear project deliverables, timelines and actions.</p></li><li><p>Identify project risks early and implement mitigation plans to protect delivery, quality and customer expectations.</p></li><li><p>Monitor project progress, budget, planning, scope and key milestones.</p></li><li><p>Support bid development, technical discussions and customer relationship management where needed.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to improving project management processes, tools and ways of working in a scaling organization.</p></li><li><p>Capture lessons learned, share knowledge and support others in building strong project delivery practices.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">What’s in it for you</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Work on products that are deployed in real-world, high-impact environments, not just concepts or internal tools</p></li><li><p>Operate in a fast-growing, international scale-up where you can truly influence how projects are run.</p></li><li><p>Regular team activities and shared lunches throughout the week.</p></li></ul> <br> <p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>What we’re looking for:</stro