-software-engineer-amsterdam-240852","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Embedded Software Engineer","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW108545368 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;">As a<strong> Senior Embedded Software Engineer</strong> at Optics11, you are responsible for the development and engineering realization of embedded software solutions throughout the product development lifecycle. You translate allocated product and subsystem requirements into robust software solutions that deliver reliable system functionality while supporting maintainability, testability, scalability, product integration, and long-term product reliability.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW108545368 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;">The embedded software subsystem comprises the software running on our sensing interrogator platforms, including <strong>e</strong>mbedded Linux applications, hardware interfaces, internal APIs, system control, calibration functionality, diagnostics, data acquisition interfaces, and supporting software infrastructure. You apply specialist embedded software expertise to develop, improve, and mature subsystem solutions that contribute to successful product realization as part of multidisciplinary engineering teams.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW108545368 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#5a5f72">You work closely with Architects, Photonics, Electronics, FPGA development, Product Integration, Verification &amp; Validation, Lifecycle Engineering, application/software teams, manufacturing, and other subsystem development teams to ensure embedded software solutions are successfully developed and realized as part of the overall product.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Key Responsibilities:</h4><ul><li><p>Develop and maintain embedded software solutions throughout the product development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p>Translate product and subsystem requirements into reliable, maintainable, testable, and scalable software designs.</p></li><li><p>Design, develop, and integrate embedded Linux applications, hardware interfaces, internal APIs, system control, calibration, diagnostics, and related software components.</p></li><li><p>Take ownership of significant software workstreams and mature existing software stacks into reliable product-level solutions.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain software testing, automation, CI/CD, diagnostics, and repeatable release processes.</p></li><li><p>Support prototype development, system integration, verification, qualification, industrialization, and product release.</p></li><li><p>Analyze system and software performance and troubleshoot complex issues across software, electronics, FPGA, photonics, and system interfaces.</p></li><li><p>Identify technical risks, evaluate design alternatives, and contribute to architecture, design, and code reviews.</p></li><li><p>Ensure software quality, reliability, security, and suitability for manufacturing, deployment, and long-term product support.</p></li><li><p>Plan and deliver assigned work against agreed priorities and milestones, proactively communicating risks, dependencies, and technical debt.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate across multidisciplinary engineering teams and provide technical guidance within your area of expertise.</p></li><li><p>Share knowledge, lessons learned, and software best practices to strengthen team capability and continuously improve engineering ways of working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em">Why Join Us?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p>Join one of Europe’s most promising deep-tech scale-ups.</p></li><li><p>Shape the future of a rapidly growing multidisciplinary R&amp;D organization.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy regular team activities and company events.</p></li><li><p>Fresh team lunches provided every day.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">BSc or MSc in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Embedded Systems, or related technical discipline.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">5+ years of relevant experience in embedded Linux software development (userspace and/or BSP).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Strong experience developing software for embedded products throughout the product development lifecycle.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Strong C++ and/or Python development skills for Linux userspace applications and services.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Strong understanding of embedded Linux, Linux application development, and hardware/software interaction.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience with software architecture, interfaces, APIs, multithreading, inter-process communication, and hardware abstraction.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience building and maintaining embedded Linux BSPs and images using PetaLinux, Yocto, or similar.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Ability to debug and patch existing Linux kernel drivers, device tree, and boot/integration issues.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience with Git, CMake, unit testing, code reviews, and modern software development practices.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience developing automated tests and contributing to CI/CD environments; familiarity with Docker in embedded development.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience with Python for automation, testing, analysis, or tooling.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Strong analytical skills and experience applying structured problem-solving and root-cause analysis methods.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience debugging complex issues across software and hardware boundaries.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Strong communication skills in English and a collaborative working style.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Eligible for required EU/NATO/security screening or clearance, where applicable to the role.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>Nice to have:</strong></h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience with Xilinx Zynq UltraScale+, heterogeneous SoCs, or comparable embedded Linux platforms.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience interfacing Linux software with FPGA-based systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Experience with real-time or high-throughput data acquisition and signal-processing systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221221344 BCX8">Hands-on Linux kernel work beyond fixes.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8">