ustify;">You own the system definition, system architecture, allocated requirements, interfaces, system-level verification intent, and technical baselines of the product. Working across multiple engineering disciplines, you ensure subsystem solutions collectively realize the intended system capabilities while balancing technical performance, manufacturability, reliability, cost, and lifecycle considerations.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;">You work closely with the Product Manager, Product Owner, Subsystem Development teams, Product Integration, Verification &amp; Validation, and Lifecycle Engineering to ensure technical decisions support successful product development and future roadmap evolution.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Key Responsibilities:</h4><ul><li><p>Define and maintain the product system architecture, requirements, interfaces, and technical baselines throughout the product lifecycle.</p></li><li><p>Translate product capabilities and roadmap objectives into clear, complete, verifiable, and traceable system requirements.</p></li><li><p>Allocate requirements across subsystems and ensure subsystem solutions collectively deliver the intended system capabilities.</p></li><li><p>Define system-level verification strategy and criteria, and support integration, verification, qualification, and product release activities.</p></li><li><p>Lead system-level technical decisions and trade-offs across performance, reliability, manufacturability, cost, risk, and lifecycle considerations.</p></li><li><p>Identify and resolve cross-subsystem technical issues, dependencies, interface conflicts, and architectural risks.</p></li><li><p>Provide technical leadership across multidisciplinary engineering teams, driving alignment, systems thinking, and continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Technical Ownership &amp; Scope:</h4><ul><li><p>Owns the system architecture, requirements, interfaces, technical baselines, and system-level verification approach.</p></li><li><p>Leads system-level technical trade-offs and assesses changes impacting system integrity.</p></li><li><p>Provides technical direction and alignment across subsystem teams.</p></li><li><p>Works within a clear scope alongside Product Management, Product Ownership, Engineering Management, subsystem teams, and V&amp;V.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#121317">Why Join Us?</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Join one of Europe’s most promising deep-tech scale-ups.</p></li><li><p>Shape the future of a rapidly growing multidisciplinary R&amp;D organization.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy regular team activities and company events.</p></li><li><p>Fresh team lunches provided 5times/ week.</p></li></ul> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">MSc or PhD in Systems Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Applied Physics, Photonics, Computer Engineering, or a related engineering discipline.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Minimum 8 years of experience in multidisciplinary product development of complex technical systems.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Demonstrated experience defining system architectures, requirements, interfaces, and technical baselines.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Demonstrated experience leading technically complex engineering work and driving technical decisions within multidisciplinary product development teams.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Strong understanding of systems engineering principles, requirements engineering, interface management, technical risk management, and verification planning.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with requirements management and systems engineering tools (e.g. Polarion, DOORS, Cameo, or equivalent).</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Strong analytical and structured engineering problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.</p></li><li><p>Eligible to obtain EU/NATO security clearance.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with optical sensing systems, underwater systems, defence, or other high-reliability products.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE).</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with architecture trade studies and system modelling.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Familiarity with configuration management and technical baseline management.</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting product verification and qualification.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please refer to details on security screening.&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/product-system-engineer-amsterdam-279660","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792009953},{"slug":"senior-mechanical-engineer-amsterdam-45815","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Mechanical Engineer","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">As a <strong>Senior Mechanical Engineer</strong> at Optics11, you are responsible for the development and engineering realization of the OptiArray system. Your primary objective is to develop robust, structural, easy to manufacture solutions that ensure the array can be easily manufactured, deployed, and operated throughout their intended service life.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You translate allocated product and system requirements into engineering solutions that provide structural integrity, mechanical robustness, corrosion resistance, manufacturability, and reliable offshore deployment.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You work closely with Product System Engineering, Product Integration, Verification &amp; Validation, Lifecycle Engineering, manufacturing partners, offshore contractors, and specialized suppliers to ensure the array is successfully developed and realized as part of the overall product.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Key Responsibilities:</h4><ul><li><p>Develop and realize robust, manufacturable mechanical and structural solutions for the OptiArray system throughout the product development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p>Translate product and system requirements into mechanical designs suitable for offshore deployment and long-term subsea operation.</p></li><li><p>Design and integrate structural components, interfaces, mounting features, lifting arrangements, and corrosion protection solutions into the overall product.</p></li><li><p>Produce engineering drawings, specifications, calculations, interface documentation, and design records.</p></li><li><p>Perform structural engineering analyses and testing, including lifting loads, fatigue, hydrodynamic behavior, environmental loads, and mechanical robustness.</p></li><li><p>Develop and evaluate prototypes and engineering models to validate structural performance and manufacturability.</p></li><li><p>Drive design improvements focused on manufacturability, assembly, maintainability, reliability, and lifecycle performance.</p></li><li><p>Support product integration, verification, qualification, FAT, and industrialization activities, resolving mechanical and structural issues where required.</p></li><li><p>Perform engineering trade-offs considering structural integrity, weight, cost, manufacturability, corrosion resistance, offshore installation, and lifecycle performance.</p></li><li><p>Work closely with fabrication suppliers, offshore contractors, and technical partners to ensure designs can be successfully manufactured, deployed, and operated.</p></li><li><p>Identify technical risks, investigate root causes, and implement effective design improvements and mitigation measures.</p></li><li><p>Provide technical guidance within the marine structures domain and collaborate across engineering disciplines to support sound technical decisions and successful product delivery.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#121317">Why Join Us?</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Join one of Europe’s most promising deep-tech scale-ups.</p></li><li><p>Shape the future of a rapidly growing multidisciplinary R&amp;D organization.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy regular team activities and company events.</p></li><li><p>Fresh team lunches provided 5 times / week.</p></li></ul> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">BSc or MSc in Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering, Marine Engineering, Offshore Engineering, Naval Architecture, or related engineering discipline.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Minimum 5 years of experience developing offshore, marine, mechanical, or structural systems.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Proficiency in working with SolidWorks or equivalent CAD systems to develop and review mechanical designs, assemblies, engineering drawings, and technical documentation.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience designing marine products, offshore equipment, or subsea mechanical systems.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience performing structural calculations, load analysis, fatigue assessment, and mechanical interface design.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience working with fabrication suppliers and manufacturing partners.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience working within multidisciplinary product development teams.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Strong analytical and structured engineering problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Eligible to obtain EU/NATO security clearance.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with corrosion protection, cathodic protection, offshore coatings, or subsea structural design.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Hands-on experience with SolidWorks for mechanical design, assembly modelling, and detailed production drawings.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience taking ownership of a system or significant technical workstream within multidisciplinary engineering projects.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Familiarity with systems engineering, product lifecycle management, verification, and configuration management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW236113144 BCX8"><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW236113144 BCX8">You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please refer to details on security screening.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-mechanical-engineer-amsterdam-45815","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792009953},{"slug":"it-director-amsterdam-395700","company_name":"Optics11","title":"IT Director","description":"<p>At Optics11, we develop ultra-sensitive fibre optic sensing technology that helps protect maritime infrastructure and energy assets around the world. We are a fast-growing, mission-driven company with colleagues from more than twenty nationalities.</p><p>As we grow, we are looking for an IT Director to lead and develop the organisation that keeps Optics11 running and ready to scale. You will shape our IT direction, strengthen service delivery and build the team, architecture and operating model needed for the next phase of the company.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>About the role</h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You will own IT strategy and delivery across Workplace and Support Services, Infrastructure, Cloud and Operational Technology, Enterprise Applications and Integration, and Product IT Operations. Your remit includes people, budget, suppliers, architecture, service management and continuity across these areas.</p><p>This is a hands-on leadership role. You will set direction and manage the team, while remaining close enough to the technology to make sound decisions and earn the trust of experienced specialists. You will introduce practical ITIL-based ways of working that make services predictable without creating unnecessary bureaucracy.</p><p>The Security Office operates independently from IT and sets security requirements, architecture input and assurance expectations. Your team will implement and operate the technical controls assigned to IT. For products in the field, Customer Service will own the customer case and Product Engineering will own product design and engineering changes. Product IT Operations will provide the specialist operational IT capability between them.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What you will do</h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Lead and develop a multidisciplinary IT team covering workplace support, infrastructure, cloud, operational technology, enterprise applications and Product IT Operations.</p></li><li><p>Own the IT strategy, architecture, roadmap and priorities, translating business needs into clear and achievable plans.</p></li><li><p>Establish an ITIL-aligned service model with one Service Desk, clear resolver groups, controlled changes, meaningful service levels and continual improvement.</p></li><li><p>Ensure the reliability and recoverability of workplace technology, identity services, endpoints, servers, cloud platforms, networks, backup and recovery.</p></li><li><p>Reduce reliance on individual experts through competent cover, documentation, secure access, knowledge transfer and tested recovery procedures.</p></li><li><p>Own the technical lifecycle of enterprise core applications and integrations, e.g. ERP, PLM, CRM. Business owners define processes and data requirements, while application champions and IT perform approved administration and changes.</p></li><li><p>Build Product IT Operations as a distinct service for the cloud, edge, connectivity and other IT components used in deployed customer products. Establish monitoring, patching, backup, secure remote access, operational readiness and clear support handovers.</p></li><li><p>Define and improve the IT responsibilities within manufacturing and test environments, including asset registration, operating systems, connectivity, support boundaries and a segregated OT network architecture.</p></li><li><p>Implement and operate the security controls assigned to IT, maintain evidence and remediation plans, and work with the Security Office on incidents, risks and exceptions.</p></li><li><p>Work with R&amp;D and Data Science on agreed infrastructure and integrations. Those teams retain ownership of DevOps and MLOps.</p></li><li><p>Plan and deliver IT services for new locations, including remote support, local hands, equipment logistics and coordination with Security and Facilities.</p></li><li><p>Own the IT budget and supplier relationships, and ensure that external partners complement internal accountability and knowledge.</p></li><li><p>Lead the disentanglement of interconnected IT services and dependencies, establishing clear ownership while protecting continuity and ensuring controlled handovers.</p></li><li><p>Use service performance, workload, risks and skills data to guide recruitment, training and investment, and communicate progress clearly to management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What we offer</h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>The opportunity to shape and scale the IT organisation of an international deep-tech company.</p></li><li><p>Meaningful responsibility for the team, services, architecture and investments within your remit.</p></li><li><p>A competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>An international working environment with colleagues from more than twenty nationalities.</p></li><li><p>Regular team activities, company events and fresh team lunches three times per week.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h4>What you bring</h4><p>We care more about what you can do than how you got there. We welcome strong candidates from different educational and career backgrounds.</p><ul><li><p>You have led an IT function or multidisciplinary technical team through growth and understand how to build capacity before services become overstretched.</p></li><li><p>You have managed specialists across infrastructure, applications and end-user support and know how to create clear ownership without losing collaboration.</p></li><li><p>You lead through coaching, practical support and honest feedback, and you invest in your team's professional development.</p></li><li><p>You are comfortable across a modern hybrid environment, including Microsoft 365, Azure and Entra ID, on-premises infrastructure, networking, endpoint management, backup and recovery.</p></li><li><p>You do not need to be the deepest expert in every domain, but you can challenge designs, ask the right questions and make credible technical decisions.</p></li><li><p>You have practical experience with IT service management, enterprise applications, integrations, architecture and technology roadmaps.</p></li><li><p>You have owned budgets and supplier relationships and can make clear trade-offs between service, risk, cost and capacity.</p></li><li><p>You have worked in, or can quickly adapt to, an environment where security, compliance and defence obligations shape how IT operates.</p></li><li><p>You communicate clearly in English with technical teams, business owners and senior management. Dutch is an advantage.</p></li><li><p>Nice to have</p></li><li><p>Experience with manufacturing IT, operational technology or segregated production networks.</p></li><li><p>Experience with operational IT services used in customer products or customer environments.</p></li><li><p>ITIL 4 or enterprise architecture training, supported by practical experience.</p></li><li><p>Experience with international office rollouts, tenant separation or organisational carve-outs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Security and compliance</h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You will work with clients in the defence and security sectors. Obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD, the Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service, is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. We will explain the process and guide you through the applicable requirements. More information you can find by: <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://english.aivd.nl/topics/s/security-screening">https://english.aivd.nl/topics/s/security-screening</a></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Ready to join us</h4><p>If you are excited to lead and grow the IT function of an ambitious technology company, we would like to hear from you. Apply through our careers page.</p><p>Optics11 is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to an inclusive environment for all employees.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/it-director-amsterdam-395700","tags":["IT"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792009953},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-amsterdam-154516","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Project Manager","description":"<p>As we continue to scale, we are looking for a <strong>Senior</strong> <strong>Project Manager, </strong>who wants to drive real impact, taking products from concept to deployment.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>At Optics11, we build advanced sensing technology that helps protect what matters most, from critical offshore energy infrastructure to underwater security systems. Our solutions operate in complex, high-stakes environments where precision, reliability, and real-world performance are essential.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>In this role, you will work at the intersection of New Product Introduction (NPI) and Field Integration, ensuring that what is developed by engineering teams can successfully operate in real-world, often offshore environments. You will play a key role in bridging the gap between development and deployment. This is a hands-on, execution-focused role in a fast-moving scale-up, where not everything is fully defined. You will need to balance structure with pragmatism, make decisions with incomplete information, and keep projects moving despite changing priorities.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">What you will do</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Lead end-to-end projects covering product delivery (hardware and software) and field integration, including offshore deployment</p></li><li><p>Coordinate across engineering, operations, supply chain, and external partners to ensure smooth execution</p></li><li><p>Translate ambiguous goals and requirements into clear, actionable plans</p></li><li><p>Drive momentum and remove blockers in fast-moving, real-world environments</p></li><li><p>Support bid preparation by building realistic timelines and execution strategies, even with limited information</p></li><li><p>Identify gaps in ways of working and proactively improve processes across teams</p></li><li><p>Enable a learning-oriented project environment by sharing best practices and coaching others</p></li><li><p>Establish feedback loops between R&amp;D and field teams to improve product and execution quality</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">What’s in it for you</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Work on products that are deployed in real-world, high-impact environments, not just concepts or internal tools</p></li><li><p>Operate in a fast-growing, international scale-up where you can truly influence how projects are run</p></li><li><p>Regular team activities and shared lunches throughout the week</p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">What we are looking for</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>5–8 years of project management experience in a technical environment</p></li><li><p>MSc degree (or equivalent) in Engineering, Physics, or a related field</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience with New Product Introduction (NPI) projects is essential</p></li><li><p>Proven track record of delivering projects with real-world execution (not only planning)</p></li><li><p>Comfortable combining structured planning with hands-on operational involvement</p></li><li><p>Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to think in a structured way</p></li><li><p>Experience with offshore or field deployment projects is a strong plus</p></li><li><p>Able to make decisions and move forward with incomplete information</p></li><li><p>Clear communicator who can align technical (R&amp;D) and operational (field) teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">You will thrive here if you</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Enjoy seeing projects come to life in the real world, not just in plans or presentations</p></li><li><p>Are comfortable navigating complexity, including on-site and offshore environments</p></li><li><p>Prefer progress over perfection and know how to balance speed with quality</p></li><li><p>Take ownership and proactively solve problems across both product and organization</p></li><li><p>Can switch between strategic thinking and hands-on execution with ease</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em">This role might not be the best fit if you</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Prefer fully defined scope and stable environments before getting started</p></li><li><p>Rely heavily on rigid methodologies or extensive upfront planning</p></li><li><p>Have worked mainly on large-scale, highly structured capital projects with limited exposure to fast-paced product environments</p></li><li><p>Prefer to stay removed from operational or field-level challenges</p></li><li><p>Find it difficult to make decisions or move forward with incomplete information</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">You'll be working with clients in the defense and security sectors, obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD (Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service) is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. For more information, please refer to details on security screening.&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-project-manager-amsterdam-154516","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792009953},{"slug":"senior-embedded-software-test-engineer-amsterdam-92032","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Embedded Software Test Engineer","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW156002957 BCX8">As a <strong>Senior Embedded Software Test Engineer</strong> at Optics11, you own the embedded software system-test capability for our sensing interrogator platforms. You define, automate, execute, and continuously improve Hardware-in-the-Loop (HIL) and box-level integration and regression testing so that software and firmware release candidates are qualified on representative hardware before they move downstream to formal verification, FAT (Factory Acceptance Test), field, or application validation.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW156002957 BCX8">Your scope covers the integrated behavior of embedded Linux applications and services, internal and external APIs, hardware interfaces, firmware and FPGA interactions, system control, calibration and configuration, diagnostics, data acquisition, boot and update behavior, recovery mechanisms, and sensor interfaces. You build and maintain automated test frameworks, HIL benches, test harnesses, CI/CD integration, and objective release evidence that make product behavior repeatable, observable, and measurable.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW156002957 BCX8">You are part of the Sensing Platform Team and work closely with Embedded Software, FPGA/Firmware, Electronics, Photonics, Architects, Product System Engineering, Product Integration, Verification &amp; Validation, Lifecycle Engineering, application/software teams, and external development partners. The primary ownership of this role is integrated interrogator/HIL system-level testing and release qualification. It complements developer-owned unit and component testing and does not replace independent formal verification, compliance, environmental, or end-to-end application validation performed downstream.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Key Responsibilities:</h4><ul><li><p>HIL &amp; System-Level Test Development</p><ul><li><p>Own the interrogator/HIL test strategy, system-level regression suite, and embedded software/firmware release qualification approach for the Sensing Platform.</p></li><li><p>Translate product, software, firmware, and interface requirements into test plans, acceptance criteria, coverage objectives, and automated regression tests.</p></li><li><p>Design, build, and maintain HIL test setups using representative hardware, simulated or real sensor inputs, and remotely controlled lab equipment.</p></li><li><p>Develop maintainable Python-based test automation for device control, test orchestration, data capture, analysis, and reporting.</p></li><li><p>Integrate hardware-based regression testing into CI/CD pipelines, enabling repeatable and largely automated testing of release candidates.</p></li><li><p>Maintain traceability between requirements, test cases, defects, results, and release evidence.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Release Qualification &amp; Failure Analysis</p><ul><li><p>Qualify embedded software and firmware releases on representative interrogator hardware before downstream V&amp;V, FAT, field, or application validation.</p></li><li><p>Design and execute system, negative, stress, endurance, fault-injection, restart/recovery, upgrade/rollback, and robustness testing based on product risk.</p></li><li><p>Analyze logs, system state, performance, timing, communication behavior, and data outputs to identify regressions and integration issues.</p></li><li><p>Triage failures and support root-cause analysis across software, firmware, FPGA, electronics, photonics, sensors, and system interfaces.</p></li><li><p>Reproduce field, production, and customer issues in laboratory/HIL environments and turn important failures into permanent regression coverage.</p></li><li><p>Provide clear, evidence-based input on release readiness, known limitations, unresolved defects, and coverage gaps.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Test Engineering &amp; Technical Ownership</p><ul><li><p>Identify quality risks, missing coverage, weak observability, testability limitations, and failure scenarios, and drive practical improvements.</p></li><li><p>Evaluate test frameworks, HIL architectures, simulation approaches, instrumentation, and automation solutions.</p></li><li><p>Work with Software, Firmware/FPGA, Electronics, Photonics, Systems, Integration and V&amp;V engineers to improve design-for-testability, interfaces, diagnostics, and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p>Own significant HIL, system-test, and automation workstreams with minimal guidance, while keeping test environments, tooling, configurations, and documentation reliable and reproducible.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to requirement, design, code, test-plan, and test-result reviews.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Collaboration &amp; Continuous Improvement</p><ul><li><p>Collaborate across multidisciplinary engineering teams to solve complex integration and product-quality issues.</p></li><li><p>Communicate test results, quality risks, defects, dependencies, and release readiness clearly to technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Share knowledge and mentor peers in embedded software testing, HIL automation, failure analysis, and robust test design.</p></li><li><p>Continuously improve automated coverage, CI/CD quality gates, test reporting, diagnostics, test-environment stability, and release processes.</p></li><li><p>Reduce flaky, manual, and repetitive testing through reusable test assets and reliable automation.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em">Why Join Us?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p>Join one of Europe’s most promising deep-tech scale-ups.</p></li><li><p>Shape the future of a rapidly growing multidisciplinary R&amp;D organization.</p></li><li><p>Competitive salary and benefits package.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy regular team activities and company events.</p></li><li><p>Fresh team lunches provided every day.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221221344 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">BSc or MSc in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Embedded Systems, or related technical discipline.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">5+ years of relevant experience in embedded software testing, embedded systems integration, test automation, HIL testing, software quality engineering, or related fields.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">Strong experience testing embedded products on physical hardware and integrated systems throughout the product-development lifecycle.</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW251310027 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">Strong Python skills for test automation, tooling, laboratory equipment control, and analysis.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW251310027 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">Strong understanding of embedded Linux systems, Linux applications and services, software processes, networking, logging/diagnostics, and hardware/software interaction.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW251310027 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">Hands-on experience designing or maintaining automated test harnesses, HIL or system-level test environments, and regression suites for embedded products.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW251310027 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW251310027 BCX8">Experience with automated test frameworks such as pytest, Robot Framework, or comparable tools; Git; Linux; Docker; and CI/CD systems such as GitLab