em-level verification and validation for complex multidisciplinary products.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You develop a strong understanding of the product, customer use cases, system architecture, operating environment, and technical risks, and translate these into effective validation strategies, test setups, and test campaigns.</p><p>The systems you validate combine sensing hardware, embedded software, Edge computing, networking, cloud software, data processing, algorithms, and customer-facing applications. Your role is therefore focused on validating the complete system and ensuring that critical customer workflows work reliably before release.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You work closely with Product, Systems Engineering, Software, Embedded, Hardware, Algorithms, Operations, Manufacturing, and other IVVQ engineers.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This is a senior hands-on individual contributor role, combining system-level thinking, test design, technical investigation, and practical validation.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h4>Qualifications</h4><ul><li><p>BSc or MSc in Systems Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Software Engineering, Embedded Systems, Physics, or a related technical discipline.</p></li><li><p>7+ years of relevant experience in system testing, verification &amp; validation, integration testing, or product qualification.</p></li><li><p>Experience validating complex multidisciplinary products combining hardware and software.</p></li><li><p>Strong understanding of system-level test strategy, risk-based testing, requirements verification, and product qualification.</p></li><li><p>Experience translating requirements and customer use cases into practical validation approaches.</p></li><li><p>Experience designing system test setups and representative test environments.</p></li><li><p>Strong troubleshooting and root-cause analysis skills across subsystem boundaries.</p></li><li><p>Working knowledge of Linu