ng>Set up Valova for each customer:</strong> You configure document types, case filtering, department rules and coding workflows.</p></li><li><p><strong>Learn from the ward:</strong> You work on site with coders and medical controlling and turn their friction into clear product requirements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Make deployments repeatable:</strong> You write the code that makes the next go-live faster: connectors, scripts, monitoring and internal tooling.</p></li><li><p><strong>Earn the hospital’s trust:</strong> You answer technical questions in security and data protection reviews (BSI C5, GDPR).</p></li></ul><h2>What we are looking for:</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Engineering experience:</strong> At least two years in software engineering, and you’re comfortable with Linux, Docker and basic networking.</p></li><li><p><strong>Integration know-how:</strong> You’ve worked on system integrations. Experience with HL7/FHIR or SAP environments is a big plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>Customer focus:</strong> You enjoy working with customers and explain technical topics clearly to IT leads and coders alike.</p></li><li><p><strong>High ownership:</strong> You move things forward, even when three parties are involved.</p></li><li><p><strong>Travel:</strong> You’re happy to spend around 30 percent of your time at hospitals across Germany.</p></li><li><p><strong>Languages:</strong> You speak fluent German and English, since our customers work in German.</p></li><li><p><strong>Location:</strong> You work from our office in Munich or Berlin.</p></li></ul><p>Missing one or two points, but convinced you’re the right person for this role? Apply anyway. We’re looking forward to meeting you!</p><h2>What you get</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Work that means something, every day.</strong> Your agents are the core of our product and directly help improve the German healthcare system.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ownership from week one.</strong> You take over real projects with a clear outcome and your