&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Location: Paris (Hybrid) | Practice Area: Technology &amp;amp; Engineering | Type: Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Imaginez et construisez des produits qui répondent aux vrais besoins des utilisateurs et transforment durablement les services financiers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco recherche des &lt;strong&gt;Product Managers&lt;/strong&gt; pour accompagner les acteurs majeurs des services financiers et de l&#39;énergie dans la conception de produits utiles à leurs clients et créateurs de valeur pour leur organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au sein de notre capability &lt;strong&gt;Tech, Product &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, vous intégrerez des équipes pluridisciplinaires réunissant Product Managers, ingénieurs, développeurs et experts métiers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Votre rôle sera de comprendre les besoins des utilisateurs, identifier les bonnes problématiques à résoudre et transformer ces insights en produits simples, viables et performants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous intégrerez également de manière pragmatique les outils d’IA et d’automatisation approuvés dans vos méthodes de travail pour accélérer la recherche, l’analyse et l’expérimentation, tout en conservant le jugement humain au cœur des décisions produit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler avec des équipes produit pluridisciplinaires pour identifier les problématiques utilisateurs prioritaires et concevoir des solutions à la fois désirables, viables et techniquement réalisables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intervenir sur l’ensemble du cycle de vie produit, de la discovery et de la recherche utilisateur jusqu’au lancement, à la mesure de la performance et à l’optimisation continue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combiner études de marché, recherche qualitative, données quantitatives et comportements observés pour construire une compréhension structurée des utilisateurs&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;et exploiter, lorsque pertinent, des outils d’IA approuvés pour accélérer l’analyse et faire émerger des insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intégrer les contraintes propres aux services financiers – réglementation, risques et contrôles, protection des données et viabilité économique – dans les décisions produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter le produit par les résultats et la valeur créée pour les utilisateurs et le business, en testant différentes approches plutôt qu’en vous concentrant uniquement sur la production de livrables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences et expériences désirées&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Au moins 5 ans d’expérience en Product Management, acquise au sein d’une entreprise technologique ou d’un cabinet de conseil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience avérée dans la discovery, la conception et le développement de produits de bout en bout, idéalement sur des expériences web et mobiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne maîtrise des méthodologies produit – Jobs-to-be-Done, personas, frameworks de priorisation, KANO, Lean Startup – et des méthodes de delivery Agile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une capacité démontrée à collaborer avec des designers, ingénieurs/développeurs, équipes métiers et parties prenantes, ainsi qu’à traiter des problématiques complexes à partir de données et d&#39;insights structurés.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne connaissance de la banque et des services financiers, associée à une curiosité pour les usages de l’IA et des workflows AI-enabled permettant d&#39;améliorer la qualité, la rapidité ou la pertinence du travail produit, dans un cadre responsable et avec validation humaine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes à l’aise pour travailler en français et en anglais dans des environnements internationaux.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi rejoindre Capco?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco est un cabinet de conseil international, spécialisé dans les services financiers.&lt;br&gt;Fondé en 1998, le cabinet compte aujourd’hui plus de 7 000 collaborateurs dans 36 bureaux à travers le monde, dont 160 à Paris.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Challenger reconnu face aux grands noms du conseil, Capco se distingue par sa double expertise métier et technologique, au service de la stratégie comme de l’exécution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre promesse : accompagner la transformation de nos clients dans un monde en constante mutation – réglementaire, technologique et opérationnel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous intervenons à l’intersection du business, de la réglementation et de la tech, en mobilisant des équipes pluridisciplinaires, expérimentées et engagées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nos marqueurs distinctifs :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une spécialisation sectorielle forte&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nous apportons à nos clients une compréhension approfondie de leurs enjeux métiers, en particulier dans la banque, les marchés de capitaux et l’énergie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une approche collaborative et sur mesure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nous intégrons les équipes clients, adaptons nos méthodes à leur culture et co-construisons des solutions concrètes et opérationnelles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L’excellence comme exigence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notre ambition est d’obtenir des résultats mesurables et durables pour nos clients – et de toujours viser la valeur ajoutée.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Un esprit “One Capco”&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nos équipes collaborent à l’échelle internationale pour mobiliser les meilleures expertises et partager les bonnes pratiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une culture entrepreneuriale et inclusive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;L’innovation, l’initiative et le mérite sont au cœur de notre modèle. Nous valorisons les idées, la diversité et le progrès collectif.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nos expertises s’articulent autour de 6 métiers complémentaires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stratégie &amp;amp; Transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance, Risque &amp;amp; Conformité&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product, Innovation &amp;amp; Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conseil Tech (Advisory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering (Delivery)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chez Capco, nous vous offrons&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un environnement de travail international centré sur l’innovation et la création de valeur pour nos clients bancaires et assuranciels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un parcours de formation continu adapté à vos besoins, pour acquérir de nouvelles compétences et développer une réelle expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une organisation de travail hybride (charte télétravail de 2 jours par semaine)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une rémunération compétitive avec un bonus lié à la performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un PEE avec un abondement de 2903€ par an&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une culture d’entreprise entrepreneuriale, inclusive et méritocratique, de nouveau certifiée Great Place To Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des initiatives pour construire le Capco de demain&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;#BeYourselfAtWork&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Woman@capco&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSE (forfait mobilité durable, jour de solidarité, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des communautés métiers, sportives et culturelles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Capco Paris, handicap visible ou invisible, parcours atypique ou classique, toutes les candidatures sont les bienvenues et seront traitées avec équité.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/capco/product-manager-h-f-173446","tags":["Innovation & Design"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1791978955},{"slug":"senior-analyst-france-netherlands-12-month-fixed-term-contract-paris-171535","company_name":"airbnb","title":"Senior Analyst, France & Netherlands (12 Month Fixed-Term Contract)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note this is a hybrid position from our Paris office. Please submit your CV in English.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Markets Strategic Finance &amp;amp; Analytics team provides budget oversight, reporting, strategic planning and analytical decision making support to the Global Markets team and in-region business teams across EMEA. In addition this team supports identifying and pursuing opportunities to drive growth and business impact for our international business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;While your formal reporting structure is into the Director, Strategic Finance &amp;amp; Analytics, EMEA, on a day-to-day basis you will work closely with the cross-functional team that is based in-region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will directly support Country Managers (and their teams) based around EMEA to drive clear reporting, produce actionable insight, track core KPIs, evaluate investment decisions and work cross-functionally to develop strategies to solve problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The individual is expected to be a strong cross-functional business partner who has a combination of hands-on analytical skills, financial modelling expertise, commercial acumen, and the ability to package their insights into strong narratives appropriate for senior executive consumption. They will be comfortable working in cross functional teams based in EMEA and around the world including Finance &amp;amp; Accounting, Business Operations, Data Science, Marketing, Product and Supply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ideal candidate relishes the opportunity to roll up their sleeves to drive meaningful impact, possess strong stakeholder management skills, and is a self-starter that is comfortable with ambiguity in a fast paced global work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This person will have a high degree of visibility with senior management within the organization, including Country Managers, Regional and Finance Leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with a Country Manager in driving performance management, including development and ongoing analysis of KPIs, creating goals/OKRs and measuring performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of what levers drive growth and efficiency for our business and translating that into investment cases and initiatives to drive business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with the business on annual planning and budgeting, laying out risks and opportunities and debating strategies and capital allocation to maximise growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stepping in to lead EMEA’s monthly business review and speaking to key drivers of variance to goal and potential actions to improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modelling and summarising the implications of a regulatory action and potential mitigating actions we could take to minimize business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Joining a call with the Regional Marketing team to discuss changes to channel or country spend and helping bridge local and regional considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digging into the regional impact of a global product feature and identifying relevant regional insights that could point to local optimization opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical deep dives: Conduct deep dives into business trends across EMEA and different segments of the business. Independently lead data extraction, analysis, visualization, and presentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build ad hoc reporting and analysis to help business operations and other cross functional partners understand the drivers of performance for key performance indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant experience. Ideally, you have demonstrated relevant experience in an analytical role such as Strategic Finance, Financial Planning and Analytics (FP&amp;amp;A), Strategy/Management Consulting, Investment Banking or Business Operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in finance, economics, mathematics, accounting, engineering, statistics or other relevant field that demonstrates quantitative orientation; MBA or advanced degree a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb financial modeling and quantitative analysis skills, SQL experience highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical abilities and able to synthesize complex information. You enjoy absorbing large amounts of data and qualitative insights and can quickly develop a strong narrative that leads to recommendations and builds our understanding of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Management: The ability to work and influence cross-functionally in a matrixed business environment is a must. You are proactive, great at communicating with different audiences and can bring stakeholders on-board. You seek out and have a track record for driving change and impact in a fluid, unstructured working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to put together clear, polished, insightful recommendations for peers, managers and senior management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re very comfortable with financial modeling in Excel, and are willing to gather internal and external data points to help build a comprehensive business case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re someone who possesses grit and finds creative ways to get the job done. You bring high energy and the ability to prioritize and deliver in a fast paced environment while balancing multiple projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Sector Experience: Experience in B2C technology businesses is preferred, particularly Marketplace/Classifieds/E-Commerce businesses; broader experience in B2B technology, including Fintech and B2B Software will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in &lt;strong&gt;English and French&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in travel and hospitality is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€64.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€75.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/airbnb/senior-analyst-france-netherlands-12-month-fixed-term-contract-paris-171535","tags":["Financial Planning and Analysis"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791978955},{"slug":"enterprise-sales-lead-french-market-paris-france-18419","company_name":"Alan","title":"Enterprise Sales Lead (French market)","description":"<h2><strong>Health can’t wait</strong>. </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not for symptoms to get worse. Not for a six‑month appointment. Not for a system to catch up. But that’s exactly how healthcare works today. You wait, until you can’t.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan exists to end the wait.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health is a universal right, and we believe this right can only become real when it’s coupled with prevention. We need to stop treating health as something we repair and start treating it as something we build, every day. It’s not solely a question of willpower. It’s the healthcare system itself that needs to work for everyone, in a sustainable way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">So we are building the<strong> new standard in prevention insurance. </strong>Alan is the first company that integrates insurance, prevention, and care into a single, acclaimed user experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are on an incredible journey to build a <strong>global leading company, with a </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers"><strong><u>unique culture</u></strong></a>. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>⭐️ Why we are hiring ⭐️ </strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re opening an <strong>Enterprise</strong> <strong>Sales Team Lead</strong> role in France to <strong>lead a growing team of 4 Senior Account Executives,</strong> who are in charge of acquiring customers <strong>with more than 3,000 employees, including all CAC40 companies.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will <strong>own acquisition on the Enterprise segment in France</strong> and <strong>run the business end‑to‑end</strong>: you will be <strong>hands-on on the field</strong> while <strong>coaching and scaling</strong> a team of Account Executives to win this market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This position sits at the heart of our growth ambition: We have just passed the one million member milestone – and this is only the beginning! We’re accelerating acquisition in France and doubling down on our portfolio — and the <strong>Enterprise segment is one of the core pillars of that plan</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Enterprise segment</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perimeter:</strong> companies of 3000+ employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Verticals:</strong> all Verticals (Tech, Retail, Industrial Companies etc)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Total Addressable Market:</strong> ~<strong>7M members</strong> in France</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Enterprise Sales is exciting at Alan</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diverse workforce</strong>: Mix of 60% cadres / 40% non-cadres, often with subsidiaries or multi-site operations, ranging from highly tech-savvy employees to those requiring digital adoption support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Critical challenges</strong>: <strong>Multi-stakeholder decision processes</strong> involving HRD, CFO, CEO, Payroll, CSE, Legal, Purchasing, Comp &amp; Ben, Accounting, Brokers, Unions, <strong>long sales cycles</strong> (multi-year conversations), RFP processes requiring deep audits and product customization, and strong influence from unions/CSE who can co-manage health insurance topics;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company profiles</strong>: Flagship companies (widely known brands), groups with standalone entities or subsidiaries, often with focus on employee wellbeing (QVT programs, Great Place to Work), modern company culture, and strategic communication about digitization or employer brand attractiveness;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR priorities</strong>: Increasing productivity, obtaining fair and competitive pricing, contributing to employee well-being through customized health plans, simplifying HR processes with digital platforms, and managing change management concerns when implementing new health insurance (biggest fear for large companies)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Critical business characteristics</strong>: This segment requires <strong>breadth &amp; depth of expertise</strong> to navigate complex organizations, <strong>account-based strategies</strong> with Key Account Management approach, early engagement in company roadmaps, face-to-face meetings, co-creation of insurance and digital products (tailored offers considering past results, specific regimes, demographics, payroll system integration), and ability to work through RFPs and with brokers. Sales cycles are <strong>volatile</strong> with high stakes: 1 deal = 50% of annual target for Enterprise Account Executives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our approach for Enterprise companies positions Alan as a <strong>strategic partner in health</strong> rather than just an insurance provider, emphasizing our digital platform for fluid UX, customized health plans at fair pricing, and health/well-being services. Success requires leveraging high-level connections, building professional materials, and potentially creating exclusive "Health Clubs" or labels for early adopters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>⭐ What you will do ⭐</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the <strong>Sales leader</strong> of the Enterprise Sales team in France, responsible for both <strong>hitting the numbers</strong> and <strong>scaling the machine</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More precisely, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the Enterprise acquisition plan in France.</strong> Design and execute the go‑to‑market strategy for 3000 employee customers, from targeting to closing, to <strong>reach ambitious acquisition targets and scale the segment</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead &amp; coach a team of 4 Account Executives</strong> (and likely more to come)</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive <strong>hiring, onboarding, and career development</strong> as we scale the crew and the segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help each team member reach their targets with <strong>clear expectations</strong>, <strong>rigorous follow‑up</strong>, and <strong>ongoing coaching</strong> on methodology, deal execution, and pipeline management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be <strong>on the field with the team</strong>: prospecting, joining key meetings, supporting tough negotiations, and owning <strong>strategic opportunities</strong> to maximize win rates.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Empower every member of the team:</strong> Create the conditions for everyone to <strong>reach and exceed their goals</strong>: strong feedback culture, coaching, clear ownership, and autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ensure market fit and remove blockers:</strong> Surface customer expectations, patterns, and blockers, and ensure they’re addressed through the right <strong>strategic and execution plans</strong> (product, pricing, ops, marketing, etc.).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the F-G<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"> <u>level range</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>⭐ Is it what you are looking for? ⭐</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You may be a great fit at Alan if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>at least 10 years experience in B2B sales</strong>, with a <strong>proven track record of hitting and exceeding targets</strong> as an Account Executive and Sales Leader</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>experience leading and coaching sales teams</strong>, with the ability to set a <strong>high bar</strong>, give <strong>clear direction</strong>, and <strong>help people grow</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have full working proficiency<strong> in French</strong>, and advanced level in <strong>English</strong> for internal communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a very <strong>hands‑on mentality</strong>: you love being on the field with your team, joining customer meetings, helping on tough negotiations, and sharing what works</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience <strong>selling to Enterprise level companies (3000+ employees and above)</strong> in <strong>multi‑stakeholder deals</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable operating in <strong>fast‑paced, ambiguous environments</strong>, and can <strong>prioritize ruthlessly</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are <strong>data‑driven and analytical</strong>: you know how to leverage KPIs to drive performance, run analyses, and make decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have strong <strong>cross‑functional collaboration skills</strong> and appetite for <strong>building things with others</strong> (sales ops, marketing, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are based (or willing to relocate to) the <strong>Paris</strong> <strong>area</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience <strong>selling to HR or Finance</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">.</p><h1>🙌   <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/about/life-at-alan/a/perks"><u>Perks &amp; Benefits</u></a></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Alan, we believe that <strong>being in good health is a basic need</strong>, and it starts with our employees. This is why Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are <strong>happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time</strong> with co-workers. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Therefore, we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fair rewards</strong>. Generous equity packages complement your base salary, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible Office</strong>. Amazing office space at our Paris HQ</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All the tools you need</strong>. Top of the range equipment: Macbook Pro, keyboard, laptop stand, monitor, and Bose noise-canceling headphones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible vacation policy and flexible working hours</strong>. Organize your time as you wish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delightful healthcare insurance</strong>. Extremely comprehensive health insurance - 100% of the contribution covered by Alan for you and your family, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transport</strong>. Country-specific commuter benefits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Training opportunities</strong>. A highly flexible Training policy free books and budget to attend and speak at conferences if the opportunity arises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental leave</strong>. Extended parental leave for all new parents, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Important note: we hire people not roles. </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">After reading this job description, if <strong>you feel like you don’t have all the necessary prerequisites</strong> but that it matches where you are now or what you'd like to grow into in your next position, <strong>we encourage you to apply</strong>!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not everybody will enter our recruitment process, but all, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply as it can only bring learnings or success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔖 Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/about"><u>About Alan</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/careers"><u>Career</u></a> pages, as well as our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://medium.com/alan"><u>Medium</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://blog.alan.com/"><u>blog</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm"><u>Glassdoor page</u></a> for more info.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alan/enterprise-sales-lead-french-market-paris-france-18419","tags":["Sales 🇫🇷"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1791978017},{"slug":"technical-delivery-manager-paris-274765","company_name":"Legora","title":"Technical Delivery Manager - Paris","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong> <br /><br />As a Technical Delivery Manager at Legora, you will play a central role in ensuring customers successfully deploy, integrate, and adopt our AI-native platform. You'll lead end-to-end technical implementations, act as the primary technical point of contact, and shape how seamlessly new customers go live and scale within Legora.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead integration projects from kickoff through go-live, owning technical documentation, test plans, and rollout execution to ensure on-time, high-quality delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the dedicated technical point of contact during implementation and early adoption, including proactive monitoring and regular stakeholder updates through go-live and the post-rollout period</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure and support customer environments including SSO, DMS integrations (iManage, SharePoint, NetDocuments), and API-based connections</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide dedicated post-rollout technical support for enterprise clients, troubleshooting advanced issues and driving high customer satisfaction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate across Sales, Engineering, and Customer Success to align on requirements and ensure a smooth rollout experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver technical training and guidance to customer teams on configuration, workflows, and best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed insights from delivery projects back to product and engineering to improve future implementations</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in technical delivery, implementation, or a similar customer-facing technical role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with SSO, authentication protocols, and enterprise integrations (DMS platforms, APIs)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent project management skills with a structured, proactive approach to managing multiple parallel projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to translate technical concepts clearly for non-technical audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator who builds trusted relationships across customer and internal teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working autonomously in a fast-paced, high-growth environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">French language proficiency is an advantage, though not a requirement for this role</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €75K – €90K</p><ul><li> • €75K – €90K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/legora/technical-delivery-manager-paris-274765","tags":["Global Services"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791978014},{"slug":"senior-fpa-analyst-paris-189795","company_name":"Aninebing","title":"Senior FP&A Analyst","description":"&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior FP&amp;amp;A Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Finance&lt;/strong&gt; team based in &lt;strong&gt;Paris&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of our Paris HQ Finance team, the Senior FP&amp;amp;A Analyst holds the full view of the company P&amp;amp;L, from net sales to EBITDA, across all channels and regions. The role combines ownership of the planning and reporting cycles with hands-on business partnering, and plays a central part in structuring our FP&amp;amp;A processes as the brand scales internationally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a rigorous, process-oriented finance professional with a strong retail background and a sharp understanding of margin mechanics. You are comfortable owning the numbers end to end and challenging the business on what drives them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;full-time permanent position (CDI)&lt;/strong&gt; based at our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;em&gt;with 4 days per week in the office and 1 day of remote work possible&lt;/em&gt;). The role reports to the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Finance&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full P&amp;amp;L ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; own the company-wide P&amp;amp;L view, from net sales through gross margin, store contribution and operating expenses down to EBITDA, consolidated across retail, e-commerce and wholesale, and across the US, Europe and Asia. Act as the go-to reference on P&amp;amp;L performance and its drivers for the Head of Finance and the leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budgeting &amp;amp; forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; lead the annual budget, monthly reforecasts and long-range plan. Own the planning calendar, key assumptions and models, and consolidate inputs from regional and functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Margin management:&lt;/strong&gt; own margin analysis at every level (channel, market, category, collection, SKU), including markdowns, promotions, cost of goods, freight, duties, FX and inventory provisions. Build margin bridges, explain variances and drive recommendations on pricing and markdown strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monthly close &amp;amp; reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; own the FP&amp;amp;A month-end close and the global management reporting package (actuals vs. budget, forecast and prior year, variance commentary, KPI dashboards). Work with Accounting to ensure management and statutory figures reconcile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business partnering:&lt;/strong&gt; serve as finance partner to Retail, E-Commerce, Wholesale, Merchandising and Supply Chain leaders on store P&amp;amp;Ls, inventory productivity and open-to-buy, pricing, promotional plans, and business cases for store openings and market entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processes &amp;amp; controls:&lt;/strong&gt; design, document and continuously improve FP&amp;amp;A processes, templates, review controls and data standards. Drive reporting automation across the finance stack (NetSuite, Excel / Google Sheets, BI tools) in coordination with Accounting and IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership support:&lt;/strong&gt; prepare materials for executive and board reviews and lead ad hoc analyses requested by the CFO and the Head of Finance. Review and guide the work of junior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5–7 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in FP&amp;amp;A, controlling or financial planning, with significant exposure to a company-wide or business-unit scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail experience is mandatory:&lt;/strong&gt; proven experience in a retail or fashion company with a store network and multi-channel model, and a solid command of store economics, seasonality, markdowns, inventory and open-to-buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full P&amp;amp;L vision:&lt;/strong&gt; hands-on experience owning or co-owning a full P&amp;amp;L, from top line to EBITDA, including consolidation across channels or countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong margin expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; gross margin building blocks, markdown and promotional impact, landed cost, inventory valuation and provisions, with the ability to explain margin drivers clearly to non-finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous and process-oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; a track record of building or improving planning, closing and reporting processes, with reliable delivery against deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel / Google Sheets and financial modeling skills; experience with an ERP (NetSuite is a plus) and a BI or reporting tool (Power BI, Looker, Tableau or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Finance, Business or Engineering, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required (global scope, US HQ, international teams); professional proficiency in French preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills: able to turn complex analyses into concise, decision-oriented messages and to challenge senior operational stakeholders with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture. Expect generous time off (including RTT), flexible work, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Style Perks: &lt;/strong&gt;enjoy a generous employee discount and seasonal wardrobe allotments — so you can live the brand, not just represent it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING seeks to empower its employees by providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, Veteran status, or other legally protected characteristics. Diversity and inclusion is critical to our success as a global brand, and we seek to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is a Los Angeles-based fashion house founded in 2012 that blends elements of Scandinavian simplicity with American energy to offer modern wardrobe essentials for women seeking a timeless yet rebellious approach to everyday style. Since its launch, ANINE BING has evolved into a global brand, available in over 90 countries with a growing network of brick-and-mortar retail stores in key cities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Powered by a global team of over 250 employees, ANINE BING is headquartered in Los Angeles and Paris, with additional offices in New York and Shanghai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Our Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located just off the Champs-Élysées, our Paris headquarters at 1 Rue François 1er is a cornerstone of our international growth. As the home of our Product teams and other key functions, this space reflects our commitment to creativity, collaboration, and global perspective. As we continue to grow across Europe, our Paris office plays a central role in shaping the future of our brand.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/aninebing/senior-fpa-analyst-paris-189795","tags":["Finance & Accounting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791968160},{"slug":"staff-product-manager-e-commerce-web-upper-funnel-cdi-lille-upline-nord-paris-paris-119818","company_name":"Decathlontechnology","title":"Staff Product Manager – E-Commerce Web Upper Funnel [CDI] (f/m/d)","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – E-Commerce Web Upper Funnel [CDI] (f/m/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localisation :&lt;/strong&gt; Paris ou Lille, France&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Équipe :&lt;/strong&gt; Decathlon E-Commerce Web – Périmètre Upper Funnel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos de l&#39;équipe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l&#39;écosystème digital mondial de Decathlon, notre équipe &lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Web&lt;/strong&gt; façonne la destination en ligne de millions de passionné·es de sport à travers le monde. Le périmètre &lt;strong&gt;Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt; constitue la porte d&#39;entrée de notre expérience digitale : de la page d&#39;accueil et la navigation par catégories, à la découverte de produits via le moteur de recherche, les recommandations IA, le commerce conversationnel, les espaces Retail Media et les contenus d&#39;inspiration. Notre mission est de guider de manière fluide chaque utilisateur de l&#39;inspiration jusqu&#39;à l&#39;intention d&#39;achat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rejoindre cette organisation Produit Web à fort trafic, c&#39;est évoluer à très grande échelle, où la vitesse, l&#39;excellence de la découverte, le SEO, la monétisation ciblée et les parcours personnalisés de nouvelle génération génèrent notre impact business quotidien.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;, tu apporteras la vision stratégique, l&#39;architecture fonctionnelle et le leadership produit nécessaires pour faire passer l&#39;expérience de découverte et d&#39;exploration de notre plateforme web à l&#39;échelle supérieure. En toute autonomie, tu traiteras des enjeux complexes : performance de la recherche, structuration du catalogue, intégration du Retail Media et virages technologiques de l&#39;IA (interfaces conversationnelles, agents autonomes).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tes responsabilités s&#39;articulent autour de 4 piliers stratégiques :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Alignement stratégique, gestion des parties prenantes &amp;amp; Vision Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Porter la vision globale de la découverte &amp;amp; de l&#39;engagement&lt;/strong&gt; : Définir et piloter la feuille de route stratégique des points de contact de l&#39;Upper Funnel (Page d&#39;accueil, Pages catégories/listes, Moteur de recherche, Arborescence/Taxonomie, Emplacements publicitaires Retail Media, Assistants conversationnels et Hubs d&#39;inspiration).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignement exécuteur &amp;amp; transversal&lt;/strong&gt; : Collaborer étroitement avec la direction business globale, les responsables merchandising, les spécialistes SEO, les équipes de monétisation Retail Media et la tech IA pour aligner l&#39;organisation sur les évolutions majeures de la plateforme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pilotage des métriques macro &amp;amp; performance du funnel&lt;/strong&gt; : Suivre et optimiser les métriques clés tout au long du parcours : Trafic organique/direct, CTR de la recherche, profondeur de navigation, taux d&#39;engagement conversationnel, rendement publicitaire (eCPM), taux de rebond, CTR vers les fiches produits (PDP) et conversion globale du haut de funnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Architecture fonctionnelle &amp;amp; Orchestration de l&#39;écosystème Web&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecte Fonctionnel·le Principal·e&lt;/strong&gt; : Définir la répartition des périmètres entre les squads web (&lt;em&gt;Search &amp;amp; Conversational Discovery, Taxonomy &amp;amp; Merchandising, Personalization/Recommendations, Retail Media &amp;amp; Sponsored Listings&lt;/em&gt;) afin d&#39;éliminer les frictions et les doublons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration étroite en Triade&lt;/strong&gt; : Travailler en synergie avec les Staff/Principal Web Engineers et les Staff UX/UI Designers pour aligner la performance frontend (Core Web Vitals), le Design System web, l&#39;architecture micro-frontend, les composants UI conversationnels et les API de recherche/ad-serving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parcours omnicanal &amp;amp; passage de relais fluide&lt;/strong&gt; : Garantir des transitions fluides depuis les canaux d&#39;acquisition externes vers l&#39;Upper Funnel web, en équilibrant la découverte organique, l&#39;assistance conversationnelle/agentique et les inventaires sponsorisés, tout en facilitant le passage vers le bas de funnel (PDP, Panier &amp;amp; Checkout).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Sparring stratégique &amp;amp; De-risking Produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partenaire et mentor stratégique&lt;/strong&gt; : Conseiller les Group Product Managers (GPM) et Product Managers (PM) du domaine E-Commerce web pour naviguer au sein des algorithmes de recherche complexes, des architectures d&#39;agents LLM, des intégrations d&#39;ad-servers et des contraintes web à très fort volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stratégies de réduction des risques (De-risking)&lt;/strong&gt; : Formuler et exécuter des boucles de validation rapides sur les concepts à forte incertitude (recherche visuelle/vocale, conseillers produits conversationnels, réapprovisionnement/bundles agentiques, placements sponsorisés).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérimentation continue à grande échelle&lt;/strong&gt; : Piloter des stratégies de A/B testing et tests multivariés à fort trafic, en équilibrant l&#39;intensité des interactions conversationnelles et la pression publicitaire face à la conversion organique (frameworks CRO, Opportunity Solution Trees - OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Élévation de la culture &amp;amp; des capacités Web modernes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership IA, Agentique &amp;amp; Monétisation&lt;/strong&gt; : Promouvoir l&#39;adoption des solutions IA cloud-natives (ex: Google Vertex AI), des frameworks conversationnels, des modes d&#39;achat agentiques et des fonctionnalités Retail Media pour amplifier à la fois l&#39;expérience utilisateur et les revenus de la plateforme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Élévation des pratiques Produit&lt;/strong&gt; : Accompagner la communauté PM vers les meilleures pratiques du web moderne (frameworks de discovery continue, optimisation de la performance technique web, décisions guidées par la donnée).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multiplicateur d&#39;impact&lt;/strong&gt; : Élever le niveau collectif de l&#39;organisation Produit en tant que leader d&#39;opinion, sans rôle de management hiérarchique direct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience E-Commerce Web à échelle (7 ans+)&lt;/strong&gt; : Solide parcours en Product Management dans la mise à l&#39;échelle de plateformes e-commerce web à fort trafic (Upper Funnel, Search, Merchandising ou Navigation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise Upper Funnel &amp;amp; SEO&lt;/strong&gt; : Compréhension approfondie des mécaniques de haut de funnel, du SEO technique, des moteurs de recherche internes, de la structuration de taxonomies et de l&#39;optimisation du taux de conversion (CRO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maîtrise de la Discovery &amp;amp; de l&#39;Analytics&lt;/strong&gt; : Pratique avancée de l&#39;analytics web (GA4/Amplitude/Contentsquare), de l&#39;A/B testing à fort volume, de la recherche utilisateur qualitative/quantitative et des Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture fonctionnelle&lt;/strong&gt; : Capacité à découper des problématiques complexes de catalogue, d&#39;ad-tech et d&#39;IA/search en stratégies d&#39;exécution claires (MVP/V0/V1).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication exécutive&lt;/strong&gt; : Excellence dans la traduction d&#39;architectures search/agentiques complexes, d&#39;enjeux de revenus Retail Media et de métriques UX en présentations synthétiques pour les dirigeants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atouts &amp;amp; Compétences technologiques clés (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pluses&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; :&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Google Vertex AI&lt;/strong&gt; : Une expérience pratique de Google Vertex AI (pour le Search, les Recommandations ou le déploiement de modèles ML/LLM) est un atout majeur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Conversationnel &amp;amp; Agentique&lt;/strong&gt; : Une bonne compréhension ou expérience des interfaces IA conversationnelles (chat/voix) et des concepts de commerce agentique (résolution autonome d&#39;intention, agents IA orientés tâches) est un fort plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail Media &amp;amp; Monétisation&lt;/strong&gt; : Une expérience des concepts de Retail Media et de la gestion publicitaire (produits sponsorisés, intégration ad-server, arbitrage rendement vs UX) est un vrai plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posture &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; : Fort pouvoir d&#39;influence sans autorité hiérarchique, capacité à s&#39;épanouir dans l&#39;ambiguïté, esprit de collaboration en Triade et empathie pour accompagner les PMs plus juniors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE NOUS T&#39;OFFRONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organisation de travail hybride&lt;/strong&gt; (basé à Paris ou Lille), 2 jours de télétravail possible par semaine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Matériel haut de gamme fourni&lt;/strong&gt; en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exposition internationale&lt;/strong&gt; : Équipe projet locale au sein d&#39;un réseau mondial, avec opportunités de carrière internationale ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Développement continu&lt;/strong&gt; : Formations internes/externes, accompagnement sur mesure et participation aux conférences du secteur ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Package de rémunération complet&lt;/strong&gt; : Actionnariat salarié, participation/intéressement, et bonus mensuels/trimestriels.&lt;/li&gt;
