&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/fanaticscommerce/head-of-operations-france-cdd-6-months-paris-187983","tags":["Commerce - International - Corporate Function"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791968159},{"slug":"remote-care-account-manager-clinical-europe-west-africa-france-106455","company_name":"Intellecthq","title":"Care Account Manager (Clinical), Europe & West Africa","description":"<h3><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p>Intellect delivers a clinically governed mental health programme to enterprise clients in the mining and resources sector, supporting remote and expatriate workforces. This is not a standard EAP. Cases begin with acute risk assessment on remote sites and run through structured treatment, fitness-for-work assessment and return-to-work clearance, in direct coordination with the client's chaplaincy, medical and people teams.</p><p>This role covers the client's United Kingdom operations and a West African project site where the working language is French. It is a combined clinical delivery and case management role: the postholder conducts the assessments, delivers the therapy, writes the reports and owns the case, rather than coordinating a provider network. That design reflects the absence of an established provider network in the West African market at launch, and gives the client a single clinician who knows each case end to end.</p><p>Full professional fluency in French and English is a non-negotiable requirement. Welfare calls, clinical assessment, case documentation and client communication in the West African market are conducted in French.</p><h3>Responsibilities</h3><p><strong>Clinical assessment and delivery</strong></p><ul><li>Conduct acute risk and welfare assessments for employees referred through the client's escalation pathway, in French or English as required.</li><li>Deliver individual counselling and psychotherapy across the supported caseload, virtually.</li><li>Conduct fitness-for-work assessments and produce the associated clinical documentation.</li><li>Write risk assessments, session documentation, return-to-work memoranda and fitness-for-work reports to a standard that stands up to client and regulatory scrutiny, in the language the case requires.</li><li>Delivery is capped so that case management availability is protected. Session load is agreed with the Head of Clinical Operations and reviewed as volume changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Case management and coordination</strong></p><ul><li>Own each case end to end, from referral through assessment, treatment, fitness-for-work and reintegration to closure.</li><li>Align the initial support plan with the client's on-site teams, including session volume and cadence, and manage adjustments where clinically indicated.</li><li>Coordinate with internal helpline, care excellence and network partnership teams on anything that cannot be delivered directly.</li><li>Review the open case list for stalled items and follow up to keep cases moving.</li></ul><p><strong>Clinical risk oversight and governance</strong></p><ul><li>Confirm risk tiering against the client's framework and set review cadence and monitoring requirements.</li><li>Make the clinical decisions the pathway requires, including disputed risk ratings and medical evaluation pathways where an employee declines therapy.</li><li>Escalate to the Head of Clinical Operations where a case exceeds the scope of remote delivery or requires in-person intervention.</li><li>Work within the differing regulatory, medical and emergency-escalation environments of each market, and flag where local pathways do not support the agreed protocol.</li></ul><p><strong>Clinical protocols and client enablement</strong></p><ul><li>Co-develop and maintain the clinical protocols, risk frameworks and SOPs the client's on-site teams operate to, including French-language versions.</li><li>Design and deliver clinical training and framework guidance to client-side staff who are not clinicians, in French and English.</li><li>Build out the in-market provider network alongside Network Partnerships, so that in-person and overflow capacity exists as the programme scales.</li></ul><p><strong>Client relationship, insights and reporting</strong></p><ul><li>Act as the named clinical contact for the client's chaplaincy, medical and health and safety leads in both markets, responding within the core window to queries that are frequently unscheduled and time-critical.</li><li>Produce the case tracker and monthly clinical reporting, moving beyond utilisation to presenting issues, risk patterns, outcomes and service-level themes.</li><li>Present clinical insight at client review meetings and translate it into recommendations the client's health and safety and people teams can act on.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Full professional fluency in French and English, to the standard required for clinical assessment, therapy delivery and client-facing documentation in both languages.</li></ul><ul><li>Registered clinical psychologist or qualified counsellor, with current registration in your jurisdiction and the right to practise remotely.</li><li>Master's degree in clinical psychology, counselling or a related field.</li><li>Minimum three years in clinical practice, including direct delivery of assessment and therapy to adults.</li><li>Demonstrable experience managing acute risk, including suicidality, in a setting where you held the decision rather than advised on it.</li><li>Experience of structured return-to-work, fitness-for-work or occupational mental health pathways.</li><li>Able to work four hours a day, Monday to Friday, within the 08:00 to 17:00 UK and West Africa window.</li></ul><p><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul><li>Experience working across multiple jurisdictions or with expatriate, rotational or multinational workforces.</li><li>Understanding of remote industrial, mining, resources or energy operating environments.</li><li>Additional language capability, particularly Mandarin.</li><li>Experience contributing to clinical protocols, risk frameworks or SOPs.</li><li>Prior case management or clinical account experience in a commercial setting.</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/intellecthq/remote-care-account-manager-clinical-europe-west-africa-france-106455","tags":["Mental Health Care","Clinical","Remote"],"job_types":["Part time"],"location":"France","created_at":1791962424},{"slug":"senior-sales-engineer-339998","company_name":"Catonetworks","title":"Senior Sales Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to the future of cloud networking and security!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Cato Networks is the first company to converge enterprise networking and security into one centralized and global service that is delivered by cloud. It is led by networking and security pioneer Shlomo Kramer (Check Point, Imperva) and early investor (Palo Alto Networks, Exabeam, Trusteer and more). Cato’s unique technology inspired a brand-new product category, later named “SASE” by Gartner and a market expected to reach $28.5 billion by 2028.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is your opportunity to get on the rocket ship and join a company that is building a cutting-edge enterprise network and secure cloud platform, and is on a fast track to becoming the worldwide market leader – don’t miss it!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
