ork across pre-sales, customer delivery, and ongoing support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in French, with the ability to work confidently with French-speaking customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to be based in France, ideally in Paris</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Required Skills</strong></h2><h3><strong>Technical Skills</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence using investigative tools and the ability to develop expertise in Chainalysis Reactor</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work with investigative data and turn customer requirements into practical workflows, queries, and reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with blockchain investigation tools or analytical workflows is an advantage; Python and SQL are not required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to learn Chainalysis products and understand how their data can support customer investigations</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Domain Expertise</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in law enforcement, policing, intelligence, financial crime, or another relevant investigative field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of investigative objectives, operational workflows, and the outcomes customers need to achieve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to use investigative judgement to guide an investigation and advise customers on their approach</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Customer &amp; Communication Skills</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to build trusted customer relationships through investigative knowledge and practical support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent spoken and written French, including the ability to explain complex investigative concepts clearly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence leading customer meetings, briefings, demonstrations, and training sessions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to help customers develop their own skills and use Chainalysis tools independently</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Day to Day Activities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct investigations using Chainalysis tools, primarily Reactor, based on customer requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare investigative reports, workflows, queries, and other analytical outputs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with customers to develop and implement investigative workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver hands-on training, walkthroughs, and knowledge-sharing sessions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead demonstrations, investigative briefings, and solution presentations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support pre-sales discussions, technical discovery, and solution scoping</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather customer feedback and share practical recommendations with Product, Engineering, and Global Intel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage multiple customer engagements while maintaining quality and responsiveness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continue developing knowledge of blockchain investigations and emerging crypto-related threats</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Personal Attributes</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about blockchain technology, crypto crime, and investigative techniques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to communicate clearly and adapt to different audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable taking ownership and making sound decisions in situations where the path forward may not be clear</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative and willing to work across teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keen to develop specialist knowledge and share it with others</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have experience: [icing on the cake, not a deal breaker]</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous experience using Chainalysis products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with cryptocurrency investigations, blockchain analytics, or financial-crime analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in traditional finance or financial investigations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience providing expert evidence or supporting legal proceedings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with compliance frameworks such as BSA/AML, sanctions screening, MiCA, or the Travel Rule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data platforms such as Databricks, Snowflake, or cloud-based analytics tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Published research, intelligence reports, or other work relating to blockchain analytics or financial crime</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Chainalysis</strong><br />AI is not a feature at Chainalysis - it is a new way of working. One that turns instructions into work done, and helps us move faster than the threats we're built to counter, and we expect our employees to take ownership of the output and ensure quality. As the world's most trusted blockchain analytics platform, Chainalysis sits at a rare intersection of proprietary data, regulatory relationships and crypto expertise that makes it uniquely placed to shape and lead the next era of AI-driven intelligence - and we expect everyone here, regardless of role, to be an active part of it.<br /><br />AI fluency is tied directly to how we measure performance and how we plan to win. There is no substitute for your own curiosity. We provide the tools, workflows, and space to experiment - but the expectation is that you develop these capabilities yourself, bring ideas, and collaborate across teams to reinvent the way work gets done. We are