le</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Senior Design Release Manager to join our Airframe Team in Lausanne. In this role, you will bridge the gap between initial mechanical concept and full-scale manufacturing, taking complete ownership of the manufacturing dossier for our composite structures and airframe modules.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From day one, you will drive Design for Manufacturability and Design for Assembly directly inside the design loop, before parts are frozen. You will set and hold the release standard, define geometric dimensioning and tolerancing, manage engineering change orders, and act as the single authority signing off on product transfer gates to manufacturing.</p><h3>What You Will Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manufacturing Dossier Ownership:</strong> Own and maintain the complete transfer package for your designated airframe module, including controlled drawing packages, bill of materials structures, material and finish specifications, critical characteristics, and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design Loop Integration:</strong> Collaborate directly with mechanical design engineers early in the design phase to optimize composite layups, bonded joints, tooling interfaces, and tolerance stack-ups while design changes are still fast and low cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transfer Gate &amp; Release Authority:</strong> Serve as the final authority on product release packages, evaluating transfer readiness against gate standards before handing hardware over to manufacturing operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Disposition &amp; Configuration Management:</strong> Manage engineering change orders and serve as the single technical contact for drawing dispositions, non-conformance reviews, and design clarification requests from the production line.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supplier &amp; Manufacturing Alignment:</strong> Work closely with production operations and external suppliers to evaluate manufacturing constraints for composite structures and precision assemblies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feedback &amp; Continuous Improvement:</strong> Analyze initial production build data and floor feedback to refine manufacturing dossiers and update gate standards for future design iterations.</p></li></ul><h3>What We Are Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background:</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://B.Sc">B.Sc</a>. or <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://M.Sc">M.Sc</a>. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Materials Science, or a related technical discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Geometric Dimensioning &amp; Tolerance Analysis:</strong> Practical mastery of applying GD&amp;T with intent, performing tolerance stack-up analyses, and defining clear acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Composite Structures &amp; Manufacturing:</strong> Strong working knowledge of composite materials, layup sequences, tooling limitations, cure cycles, and bonded structural joints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drawing &amp; Package Control:</strong> Proven experience owning released drawing packages, managing structured bill of materials, and running engineering change order workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early Stage Execution:</strong> Demonstrated success integrating manufacturing and assembly principles directly into active design reviews rather than conducting post-design audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language Skills:</strong> Professional proficiency in both English and French to work fluidly across design engineering and French-speaking production teams.</p></li></ul><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct ownership in defining the release and manufacturing transfer standards for high-performance defense airframes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active collaboration with design engineers early in the development cycle where engineering decisions carry high leverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-visibility technical impact across fast-scaling, hardware-centric production programs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/design-release-engineer-airframe-lausanne-97765","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1791859214},{"slug":"validation-technician-lausanne-148133","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Validation Technician","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Drone System Validation Technician &amp; Remote Pilot</strong>, you will be a vital pillar of our flight operations. You will ensure that our fleet of autonomous drones remains operational, up to date, and ready for deployment at all times. You will manage the validation lab and support engineers during complex field testing campaigns.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><h3>Fleet Maintenance</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform preventive and corrective maintenance on the drone fleet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carry out repairs, upgrades, and component replacements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute soldering, wiring, and mechanical assembly operations.</p></li></ul><h3>Flight Operations</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Piloting drones during test campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the safety operator during test flights.</p></li></ul><h3>Logistics</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage inventory for spare parts, batteries, and field equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organize transport and gear preparation for field testing campaigns.</p></li></ul><h3>Test Execution</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run standardized test protocols and checklists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report results and anomalies to the engineering teams.</p></li></ul><h3>Lab Management</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the workshop and validation lab clean, organized, and secure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure all necessary tools, consumables, and equipment are available and ready to use.</p></li></ul><h2>Candidate Profile</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical degree or significant practical experience in electronics, mechanics, or RC modeling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong manual dexterity: proficient in soldering, wiring, and mechanical assembly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous, organized, and safety-conscious mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience piloting multirotor or fixed-wing drones (remote pilot certification is a plus).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interest in hands-on DIY / technical building projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English language proficiency: A2 level minimum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel for field testing operations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/validation-technician-lausanne-148133","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1791859214},{"slug":"characterization-lead-saint-sulpice-168976","company_name":"Kandou Ai","title":"Characterization Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>Kandou</strong>, we are redeﬁning the economics of AI infrastructure. Our mission is to <strong>democratise AI by signiﬁcantly reducing the Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) </strong>of hardware systems — a critical barrier to scalable adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our proprietary <strong>MIMO-over-copper technology </strong>powers a <strong>high-performance, chiplet-based AI memory fabric </strong>that is both <strong>scalable and energy-efficient</strong>. Unlike traditional interconnects, our solution <strong>reduces power consumption signiﬁcantly </strong>while preserving <strong>high bandwidth and ultra-low latency </strong>— unlocking unprecedented efficiency for AI training and inference at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Characterization Lead,</strong> you will own performance characterization of Zinal retimer silicon and the Randa Active Electrical Cable (AEC) channel. This is a Principal / Senior Staff individual contributor role with hands-on technical leadership. Your measurements will establish datasheet limits, channel classes and guard-bands for validation, manufacturing and customer specifications. Based primarily in Lausanne, you will work with silicon, signal integrity and validation teams, including channel characterization partners in Taiwan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsabilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Lead silicon and channel characterization from measurement planning and bench setup through analysis, limit derivation and documented hand-off to validation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Characterize TX/RX SerDes performance across process, voltage and temperature: swing, jitter, sensitivity, equalization, adaptation, CDR lock, BER bathtubs and shmoos.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Own channel measurements to at least 50 GHz, including de-embedding, insertion/return loss, mixed-mode S-parameters and common-mode and mode-conversion behavior.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Establish reference-paddle baselines and channel classes by gauge, reach and frequency; correlate HTDR-derived metrics with calibrated VNA measurements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Derive datasheet limits and guard-bands from measured distributions, accounting for uncertainty, sample coverage and aging; maintain traceable datasets and limit revisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Assess carrier-loading and forwarded-clock tradeoffs using measured channel data and simulation, and translate the findings into supported configurations and characterization limits.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Characterize power, energy per bit and thermal behavior across operating modes and corners; investigate equalizer noise amplification and channel/thermal interactions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Coordinate shared laboratory equipment and characterization milestones with validation teams; lead technical reviews and deliver limits in time for downstream qualification and screening.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential Experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· 10 to 14 years of experience in SerDes/silicon characterization and/or high-speed channel and signal integrity characterization following degree completion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Direct ownership of a characterization program whose results became datasheet limits or qualification thresholds for a shipping product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Strong VNA measurement experience to 50 GHz or beyond, including de-embedding, mixed-mode S-parameters (Sdd/Scc/Scd/Sdc) and insertion/return-loss mask interpretation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Hands-on TX/RX SerDes characterization, jitter decomposition, BER bathtubs, PVT shmoos and equalization/adaptation analysis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Demonstrated common-mode and mode-conversion measurement depth, with the ability to distinguish channel behavior from fixture and calibration artifacts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Statistical characterization and guard-band derivation across corners, with clear treatment of measurement uncertainty, sample size and aging.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience with VNAs, oscilloscopes of at least 50 GHz bandwidth, BERTs, jitter instrumentation, thermal forcing and ATE characterization load boards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· BS in Electrical Engineering or equivalent, with the technical communication and coordination skills to hand off defensible limits to validation and manufacturing teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential Experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Characterization leadership for shipping 100G/lane or 200G/lane retimers, PHYs, AECs or AOCs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Deep mixed-mode characterization where common-mode behavior affects information transport and link margin.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience producing datasheet limits that a separate validation team independently qualified.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Multi-carrier or proprietary coding schemes, including OFDM-style subcarriers and space-time coding, and their characterization implications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Published work or patents in channel modeling, de-embedding or SerDes characterization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· MS or PhD with a concentration in communications, RF/microwave engineering or signal integrity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this is the role you have been looking for and you want to be part of a growing Company, with an exciting future then we would love to hear from you. Together We Kandou It!!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/kandou-ai/characterization-lead-saint-sulpice-168976","tags":["RnD - Lab"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Saint-Sulpice","created_at":1791859212},{"slug":"business-development-representative-bdr-zurich-151452","company_name":"Rivia","title":"Business Development Representative (BDR)","description":"<h2><strong>About Rivia</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://rivia.com/">Rivia</a> is a data engine for clinical trial intelligence. It provides data infrastructure and AI-driven workflows for clinical trial teams, enabling biotechs to run studies more efficiently and to demonstrate which patients derive the greatest benefit from new therapies. Biopharma companies are the source of most therapeutic innovation, yet clinical development is frequently slowed by fragmented data and outdated tooling. Rivia delivers a real-time, integrated view across clinical trial data, improving both trial execution and the evaluation of new treatments.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our goal is for Rivia to become the new standard infrastructure for modern drug development, bringing new therapies to market more successfully at a fraction of the cost.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We seek highly driven, motivated and talented professionals to contribute to our growing startup.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>About Rivia's Sales Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Sales team is at the forefront of Rivia's growth, bringing innovative clinical trial technology to biotech and pharmaceutical companies across Europe and the US.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate in a complex, high-value B2B environment, where understanding customers, building trust, and creating meaningful relationships are essential to success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we scale, we're building a high-performing commercial organization that combines ambition, strategic thinking, and relentless execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Business Development Representative at Rivia, you will be a driving force behind our growth, identifying, engaging, and creating opportunities with biotech and pharmaceutical companies across Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a role where you'll simply follow a predefined playbook. You'll help build and continuously improve our outbound engine, experimenting with new approaches, identifying untapped opportunities, and finding creative ways to connect with the right decision-makers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own your prospecting activities from initial research and outreach through qualification and handover to our Account Executives. You'll develop a deep understanding of the clinical trials industry, our customers' challenges, and how Rivia can create meaningful value for their organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who is ambitious, commercially sharp, and relentless in pursuing results. Someone who moves fast, takes ownership, learns quickly, and isn't discouraged by rejection. You'll need to be comfortable navigating complex organizations, engaging senior stakeholders, and finding ways to open doors that others can't.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with our Account Executives and commercial leadership, contributing directly to our pipeline generation strategy and the evolution of our go-to-market approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by the opportunity to build, experiment, exceed ambitious targets, and have a direct impact on the growth of a Series A startup, we'd love to meet you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working Model: This role is based on-site in our Zürich office.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What Excites You</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building something from the ground up. You enjoy creating and improving outbound strategies rather than simply executing an established playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The challenge of opening doors, engaging hard-to-reach decision-makers, and turning cold prospects into meaningful business opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working in a fast-paced, high-performance environment where ambitious targets, ownership, and measurable results drive your success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding complex industries, learning about customers' challenges, and connecting innovative technology to real business needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experimenting with different prospecting approaches, messaging, and channels to discover what works and continuously improve results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with Account Executives and commercial leadership, contributing ideas and challenging assumptions to improve our go-to-market strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being part of an ambitious startup where your individual contributions directly influence company growth and commercial success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taking ownership of your results, pushing through challenges, and continuously raising the bar for yourself and the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Outbound Prospecting &amp; Pipeline Generation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own outbound prospecting activities, identifying and engaging potential customers across biotech and pharmaceutical companies in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and execute targeted, multichannel outbound campaigns through email, LinkedIn, cold calling, and other creative approaches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research target accounts, map key stakeholders, and identify relevant decision-makers and influencers within complex organizations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generate and qualify high-quality sales opportunities, ensuring a consistent pipeline of relevant prospects for our Account Executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop personalized outreach strategies that connect Rivia's value proposition to prospects' business challenges and priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take accountability for individual activity, meeting, and qualified pipeline generation targets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial Strategy &amp; Market Intelligence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to building, testing, and optimizing our outbound strategy, identifying new segments, opportunities, and approaches to improve pipeline generation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Account Executives to define target accounts, qualification criteria, and effective handover processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop a strong understanding of the clinical trials landscape, including biotech business models, clinical development challenges, and industry trends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather insights from prospect conversations to identify market opportunities, refine messaging, and strengthen our commercial positioning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Sales, Marketing, and Product teams to improve campaigns, customer understanding, and go-to-market effectiveness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Execution &amp; Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and maintain accurate prospecting data, activities, and pipeline information in our CRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and analyze prospecting performance, including outreach effectiveness, conversion rates, and pipeline contribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously experiment with new messaging, tools, and outreach strategies to improve results and increase efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively identify bottlenecks, challenge ineffective approaches, and implement improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to building a high-performance sales culture based on ownership, collaboration, continuous learning, and accountability.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What Excites Us</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 2 years of experience in B2B outbound sales, business development, or sales development, ideally in